{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs","id":1460472,"title":"[World-Building] How do you do the Anarchs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-19T15:15:40-07:00","id":1460472,"title":"[World-Building] How do you do the Anarchs?","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a>'s excellent post on the subject in the Sabbat thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380845-v5-the-sabbat-in-v5?p=1460463#post1460463\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...63#post1460463</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You make it sound like a bad thing?<br /> <br /> But, uh, no. But also Yes. Depends on the cities.<br /> <br /> In some cities, the Cam is strong, the sense of community is strong, and resistance is futile. Many vampires don't know that they have a choice: There are no open anarchs, so someone with different ideas is going to find no allies, and with an absence of information, they're going to come to believe that all cities are like this. Suicides are a hundred times more likely than an anarch popping up, and if someone does start causing problems, it's very easy for the Camarilla to trick the neonate into breaking a law and destroying them with a good pretense.<br /> <br /> Because political horror is fun to me.<br /> <br /> In other cities, the Cam is certainly strong, but the community is unstable. Nobody is strong enough to declare themselves an Anarch openly, but there are certainly people who hate the prince or covet his title, or they may hate or covet the resources of other powerful vampires. Some may grow to hate the Camarilla as an institution, and may very much desperately wish to get rid of it, but openly fighting will turn your domain into free real estate.<br /> <br /> Because again, Political horror is fun to me.<br /> <br /> In <i>other </i>cities, the central authority isn't strong or agressive enough to scare people out of calling themselves anarchs, but they basically act as little more than an opposition party that never wins in a democratic country. Oh yes, there might be some covert warfare in there, and a little bit of &quot;We'll fight you if you actually make this rulling&quot; and they otherwise mostly agree to follow the Prince's laws so long as he doesn't pull bullshit on them. They might have some more autonomous regions.<br /> <br /> and in still other cities... The Cam exists, but there's more anarchs, and the Cam largely survives because they're the least offensive faction, they're good at playing the Anarchs against eachother , or more likely the Anarchs are fighting eachother on their own vollition.<br /> <br /> If a cities goes completely Anarch, well, it's like Communism. If it's doing poorly, the Cam will hold it up as an example of why it should never be done. If done well, the Cam will hold hands with the Sabbat and start skipping into the city with flamethrowers in tow. </div> </div> </div>I'm curious how you do your Anarchs.<br /> <br /> What's their relationship to the Camarilla, size, and power?<br /> <br /> How relevant are they?<br /> <br /> And other bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T15:26:11-07:00","id":1460473,"title":"","content":"My take on the Anarchs is that they're two very different groups between V1 to V20 and V5.<br /> <br /> <b>V1 to V20</b><br /> <br /> The Anarchs are simultaneously a safety valve and a source of continuous pressure on vampire society from the Convention of Thorns onward. The idea behind their &quot;legality&quot; in the Camarilla seems like it would have been a mistake from such seasoned players of the game. However, by making the Anarchs legal as a political position, the Camarilla was able to keep an eye on the trouble makers and also co-opt or divide them.<br /> <br /> As much as the Camarilla gets shit for being &quot;The Man&quot;, the fact was the Camarilla actually made some valid concessions. In my games, the Traditions were actually an improvement over how vampires were previously treated. Before, a sire could destroy their progeny at any time for any reason and the same for the ruler of a domain. Most of them were blood bound from the beginning and sires had &quot;pyramids&quot; of slaves ranging from the Eldest to the Youngest. If the Blood Bond wasn't illegal, it certainly had a lot more stigma to be attached and you were only supposed to use it as punishment or between lovers. The Tremere being an exception because who gives a fuck about the Tremere.<br /> <br /> This philosophy of &quot;divide, coopt, and conquer&quot; didn't always work as the French Revolution, Russian Revolution, and the American Revolution (which was as much Sabbat as Anarch) showed. Then the whole business of losing California to Jeremy MacNeil and his rabble. Things like the Council Wars also showed that the Anarchs were not a cat that was particularly belled. Still, the Anarchs chief benefit is the fact that it gave the impression that Princes could be opposed without being overthrown. A gang of Anarchs protected each other and made it so automatically killing them wasn't an option even if a Prince wanted to. It made tensions always exist in a city but that <i>wasn't a bad thing</i> according to most Princes.<br /> <br /> Usually, Anarchs in the Camarilla were made of Neonates or Ancilla with the latter eventually &quot;selling out&quot; and joining the Establishment. The Brujah EstablishmentTM was a major pillar of the Camarilla as they were people who claimed to be fightng the Good Fight even as they were every bit as involved in the politics as any Ventrue. This helped decapitate the Anarchs of leadership as eventually the best and smartest became Camarilla stooges or stuffed shirts even if they publicly said they were resisting the Prince or fighting for the rights of the young.<br /> <br /> You see, as long as the worst troublemakers in a city were gathered together in a gang, that helped make a Prince look relevant. Many Princes suffered the Anarchs and things they could order them to be destroyed for because that reminded the Elders and Ancilla of a city why there were threats. Most would never plan to go on a killing spree or diablerie but the distant possibility made more Princes secure than overthrew them.<br /> <br /> Only rare were the Princes so tyrannical and insane like the Prince of East Berlin that they destroyed all Anarchs and people seeking &quot;freedom&quot; or &quot;protection.&quot; Those actually became the ones the Anarchs sought to truly overthrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T15:36:53-07:00","id":1460474,"title":"","content":"<b>V5</b><br /> <br /> What killed the Anarch/Camarilla detente was not any grand act of tyranny on behalf of the Camarilla or some great victory on the part of the Movement. Instead, the big issue that changed everything was the Anarchs becoming more like their enemies.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition, Gehenna Wars, and Beckoning may not have destroyed the old vampire society but it created a power vacuum that made a lot of positions open that would previously have required decades or even centuries of careful maneuvering to acquire. Instead, it became possible for gangs of Anarchs to take over cities directly and declared themselves &quot;Barons&quot; (Princes with another name). The Camarilla was too pressed to smash all of these down.<br /> <br /> Without the carrot of the Camarilla's power, many leaders saw the opportunity to use the Anarchs as a legitimate alternative to Camarilla power and build their own mini-kingdoms. Marcus Vitel in Washington D.C. is as much an autocrat as any vampire alive but happy to bribe his minions into obedience. California was retaken after the Kuei-Jin were driven out and Camarilla retreated. Berlin fell because the Camarilla DID decide to remove a well-liked Prince for not being &quot;hard&quot; enough. Also, the Thin Bloods were now numerous enough and dangerous enough to be their own Anarch faction.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Anarch Movement&quot; is partially propaganda from the Ministry that is making alliances between various Anarch domains. The Gangrel and Brujah having &quot;left&quot; the Camarilla was always hyperbole even if neither of them have Inner Council members or Justicars anymore. However, it makes the Anarch Movement seem more powerful and dangerous, which serves both sects. What it really is, is a vague support network of information and resources to prop up the web of tiny kingdoms the Camarilla has withdrawn from.<br /> <br /> Most cities are like Chicago where there's the Anarchs &quot;ruling&quot; a area right outside the proper city while doing their business in the city with only occasional harassment from the Sheriff and Deputies.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the biggest change from V20 to V5 is the fact that in most cities there's no change at all. Princes have declared &quot;Red Zones&quot; where Anarchs may feed freely and other independents and this is coincidentally the territory held by them. Anarchs generally shout a lot about Camarilla oppression but stay out of &quot;enemy territory.&quot; Plenty of vampires on both sides still associate as before and ignore politics.<br /> <br /> But it's very convenient to have rivals and people to blame when things go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T16:08:58-07:00","id":1460476,"title":"","content":"Like a lot of things, this also varies by edition.<br /> <br /> In <b>1e</b>, Anarchs and the elders are the two main factions in the game. They're both assumed to be members of the Camarilla and PCs are assumed to be Anarchs. There are several adventures that actually say &quot;the Anarchs&quot; in place of &quot;the PCs&quot;. Anarchs vs. elders is the main external conflict in the game. <i>Chicago by Night </i>is all about Anarchs vs. elders. Anarch wars basically define the city's history from the 1910s and onwards. The latest Anarch war in the '80s defined the city current political landscape. Yet for all the narrative focus on Anarchs, they are impotently raging against the machine. Maldavis' coup only got as far as it did with elder help and then collapsed when Lodin submitted to... his own elders, who are pawns for methuselahs. The Anarchs' new leader post-Maldavis relies heavily upon the &quot;advice&quot; of an elder who's blood bound to a methuselah. In the end, the older vampires will usually win. This is why so many Anarchs sell out.<br /> <br /> In <b>2e</b>, the Sabbat got introduced as the cooler edgier antagonists (and alternate protagonists). The independent clans got more fleshed out. We also got rules for playing elders (<i>Elysium: The Elder Wars</i>), there was more focus on crossover, there was the mess that was the Tal'Mahe'Ra, and the game as a whole got more gonzo. Raging against the machine was no longer the game's driving conflict; the Jyhad was, and PCs could belong to more or less any side of it, and could play neonates or ancillae or elders as they preferred. <i>Giovanni Chronicles</i> put PCs in the front and center of a pivotal (albeit heavily railroaded) moment in the World of Darkness and Count Jocalo basically operated like a Bond villain. The Anarchs still existed, but writers weren't really focusing on them anymore, and they didn't occupy a significant place in any of the era's By Night books. Apart from L.A. by Night, which went out of its way to paint the Anarchs in a negative light and emphasize what a failure the Free States were. The Anarchs were just sort of &quot;there&quot;. They were the Camarilla's loyal opposition and honestly less interesting than all of the new factions being introduced. There was also less impetus for PCs to <i>be</i> Anarchs, because you could carve out a place for yourself if you did well enough in the Jyhad serving an elder patron. Sure, you'd still be someone's pawn, but you could have way more power than any Anarch PC in 1e.<br /> <br /> <b>Revised</b> toned down the game's gonzo-ness and put more emphasis on imminent Gehenna and the related sectarian wars. The Anarchs got dumped on hard. The Free States collapsed under invasion by the Wan Kuei. Thin-bloods and the Unbound movement in that book (even though it never came up beyond that book) stole a lot of their thunder. They were viewed as impotent rebellious children and treated with contempt by the setting's elders and the game's writers alike. They were part of the &quot;vagrant problem&quot;, just like thin-bloods. All of the factions introduced in 2e got a lot more love. There was also less incentive to <i>be</i> an Anarch than ever. <i>London by Night</i> had an &quot;experienced primogen&quot; who was 50 years dead. <i>New York by Night's</i> basic premise is &quot;your chronicle's coterie decides the prince, maybe even becomes prince&quot;. Anarchs were largely extraneous to the setting.<br /> <br /> <b>V20</b> went out of its way to depict a revitalized and meaningful Anarch Movement. <i>Anarchs Unbound</i> is one of the best books in the line (IMO) and says that yes, the late '90s and early aughts were a dark time for the Movement, but it makes sense! Those two decades were a prosperous time for a lot more people and there was less anti-establishment sentiment then. (This is probably why the writers didn't focus on them as much, too.) The Great Recession and subsequent Occupy movement changed all of that. The Anarchs rode that tide of anger against The Man to inflict some pretty serious blows against the Camarilla and L.A. is back in their hands. (I think this works best if one assumes the PC in <i>Bloodlines</i> either went Anarch or independent.) As far as individual games, the devs basically encouraged groups to play whatever they wanted to play, but made sure the Anarchs would be fun to play if you wanted to play them. They even got their own magic in<i> Rites of Blood</i>. The Anarchs are still the underdogs in any conflict against the Camarilla, but they are underdogs you can root for and who can pull off real wins (at least on a local scale)<br /> <br /> In <b>V5</b>, the Anarchs are more powerful than ever. The Camarilla has downsized its ranks and anyone not in the Camarilla (which now functions more like Requiem's Invictus), Sabbat, or one of the more structured independent clans is an Anarch by default. House Carna are Anarchs. The Brujah, Gangrel, and Setites are mostly Anarchs after the first two clans got expelled from the Camarilla. Thin-bloods, who are also a stronger force, are Anarchs. Add in the Beckoning on top and they are deadly serious rivals to the Ivory Tower rather than scrappy underdogs. If V20's Anarchs are the Rebel Alliance vs. the Galactic Empire, V5's are the Alliance of Free Planets vs. the post-Palpatine Galactic Empire. Sure, the Empire controls Coruscant and is still in charge, but the underdogs have won such resounding victories they might not stay the underdogs. Whether or not these were well-written changes is a separate topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like in the last thread, I prefer V20's take. I like my Anarchs to be meaningful threats to the Camarilla, and treated seriously rather than as jokes (no thanks, Revised) or afterthoughts (no thanks, 2e), but I prefer them as the scrappy underdogs (no thanks, V5) and don't want them to completely dominate the focus of the setting either (no thanks, 1e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T17:43:29-07:00","id":1460483,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, while House Carna has anarachs among her number she and her house are still Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T18:32:27-07:00","id":1460487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460483#post1460483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, while House Carna has anarachs among her number she and her house are still Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense. They were Anarchs when it was that or death at the hands of the Camarilla but with the Council of Seven gone, the Loyalists can't go after them directly and the rest of the Camarilla couldn't care less about their feud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T18:57:05-07:00","id":1460489,"title":"","content":"In the chronicles that I run, most &quot;Anarchs&quot; aren't actually Anarchs. The vast majority are simply neonate vampires who don't have power or Status, but compete against the elders/status quo. More often they not, they do this simply by <i>ignoring</i> Status which is a big no-no in vampire society. Their plots and intrigues aren't too different than those of elders, but lack their subtlety or framing. They just got more gumption than other neonates and/or lack the prudence to play smart. Some of them are targeted for whatever reason by one of the elders, and they end up in this group by choice of their own. There are also those who are the children of Anarchs and end up &quot;inheriting&quot; their position (meaning it was not really their choice; they'd end up differently if they simply have another sire). In other words, they don't choose to be. For whatever reason, they're designated that. Many of these vampires will eventually integrate into Camarilla society as they grow older, understand vampire culture better, and begin playing the game as it should be. Some though will embrace the Anarchs, primarily because they'll get oppressed too much because of the label. I'll call them Fake Anarchs, but that is an OOC designation not anything IC. Fake Anarchs can often be found as hangers on to the other types. CbN characters that fall into this category would be Damien, Neon, Travis Fett, Priscilla Gibbs, Elucid, and Derrick Stack.<br /> <br /> Another group of &quot;Anarchs&quot; are the outright criminals of vampire society. They'd be considered criminals in any kind of vampire society. But they have the label of Anarchs because 1) the elders want to discredit the Anarchs, 2) the Fake Anarchs don't know the different either, and 3) many of the political/true Anarchs are either fools who get conned or see them as useful tools. CbN examples include Gengis, Gordon Keaton, Dickie Fulcher, and Dooley.<br /> <br /> Then we get into the &quot;real&quot; Anarchs. These are people who want and embrace the label. But even here there are divisions.<br /> <br /> The first group is what I call &quot;Poser Anarchs.&quot; They really don't want to overthrow the system. That's too dangerous and too much work. Instead, they simply want power, prestige, and influence they can't get in Camarilla society for whatever reason, and find those opportunities among those outside of it. Juggler is the poster boy here. When push comes to shove, they'll do just enough to maintain their street cred, but otherwise won't do anything.<br /> <br /> There are also &quot;Revenge Anarchs.&quot; They joined the cause out of a desire for revenge against a single vampire (or perhaps a small group of them). If they ever achieve their vengeance, who knows what will happen to them. They might stay as Anarchs, or drop out. Frenchie from CbN would be here.<br /> <br /> Then there are the &quot;I don't like the Prince of this City Anarchs&quot;. They THINK they are the &quot;real&quot; Anarchs, but really just don't like the local Prince. And there's a difference. Maldavis is in this category, although she would think she's in the next. There is very good evidence that her antipathy towards Lodin is a result of Critias and Annabelle (she is likely partially blood bonded to both of them) and their manipulations. Hank Cave is another one.<br /> <br /> Last are the Political Anarchs. These are the only ones who truly desire to overturn the Camarilla. The Socialists coterie of Hinds falls into this category (Hinds, Jurgis, Blackjack and Karl) - though I will also mention that Modius is part of their coterie and he clearly is not an Anarch, but someone who likely sees himself as a kind of &quot;reformer&quot; in the Camarilla. Anita Wainwright would be in here. Moving away from CbN, a lot of the famous Anarchs that define the movement are here as well (Jeremy MacNeil, Crispus Attucks, etc.)<br /> <br /> If you look at the CbN coterie charts what will be apparent is that for the most part, these do not line up as factions. Most of the Anarch groups are a mix of these. And they are not fixed categories, a vampire can start in one group and transition to another as part of their life experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> Talking from an IC perspective, you can divide the Anarchs into three groups. The first is the real Anarch movement who are trying to overturn the whole system. They are a minority, they have a lot of powerful elders and influential vampires on their side. I would arbitrarily put them at 20% of all Anarchs (and this group is heavily divided as there are many different factions based on the kind of political ideology each holds, and they see each other as rivals). The second are local groups of &quot;fuck the Prince&quot; who don't care about anything outside their city. I'll give them 40% arbitrarily as well. The last are those vampires who have the label Anarch but aren't doing anything to promote the Anarchs. Doing the math, this is another 40%. Your percentages may be different. Again, each of these factions are divided among the breakdown above.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the &quot;Anarchs&quot; are a rather dubious group. That makes it great for an ST who can have a ton of variety of motives, personalities, and goals. That means you can have any kind of experience you like in a specific chronicle set in a specific city. But they are NOT a &quot;sect&quot;. They don't have any common organization, leadership, or even common goal. SOME Anarchs lead organizations that are truly organized enough to be label a sect, but they are rather small. But if their membership is impassioned, have strong leadership, and have any powerful &quot;elder anarchs&quot; supporting them, they are capable of some success. Anarch is simply a convenient label that just as often conceals as it does reveals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T05:39:16-07:00","id":1460515,"title":"","content":"I think generally what makes a vampire go Anarch or not isn't the Prince being a dick, but the clan, or the &quot;family&quot;. Raising an Anarch is something of an embarrassment for everyone involved. Smart sires will act almost like a real parent, appearing invested in their childer's success even if the childer was only embraced to be a tool. If the sire can't convince the childe of their sincerity, they can use the blood bond to keep the child in line for at least as long as it takes the child to properly adapt to the cam (&quot;It was for your own good&quot; would probably work)<br /> <br /> Going some of the more notable clans: The <b>Ventrue</b> (I'll try not to blow my horn too much on them because I'm overly bothered by people thinking I'm a blue-blood fanboy) have some of the lowest Anarch rates because <i>usually</i> they care about their image as a collective, but also, Ventrue have a severe weakness that really encourages them to work together and pool resources. If a Neonate needs a small grant of 3 million dollars to get off the ground, they'll give it to him, 3 million is nothing to them now but it'll make that neonate extremely grateful, invested in clan's supportive culture, and ultimately that neonate will likely expand the scope of the clan's pool: even if it doesn't work, he'll still be loyal for the support. The <b>Nosferatu</b> see themselves as a world apart from other vampires, so naturally they'll band together closely. The <b>Malkavians</b> are a support group, though the rare victimizer may drive a malkavian out, or a neonate may be too much to handle, the shared sympathy . <b>Clans with stronger weaknesses have lower anarch rates, because they are more dependent on one another. </b>The interesting example is the <b>Lasombra</b>, who feel they basically have to kill the characters that can't meet standards because widespread knowledge of their weakness would be bad for all of them, so anyone who can fall into an enemy's hands has to die*.<br /> <br /> (Lasombra low-key one of the smartest written clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Clans with weaker weaknesses tend to have a weaker cohesion and thus more Anarchs</b>. The<b> Toreador</b> don't need eachother, there's certainly benefits to them banding together, but they can band with anyone and make just as good a friend with someone outside the clan; they don't really have a strong identity. Why support a struggling Toreador if it'd put you at odds with a well-to-do Malkavian, or a stronger Toreador that thought they didn't like the neonate's style? They're very much a &quot;Me&quot; clan. The <b>Brujah</b> are interesting because their weakness is actually pretty bad, but they're also a clan that thrives on conflict so they have a lot of disagreements. Thus, Brujah shelter eachother from outside persecution, but don't actually try to support one another all that much. They aren't much inclined to help eachother succeed in the Camarilla (at least if there's a disagreement, if they are on the same page, they'll be best friends, but that disagreement will come eventually) but they will tell the Prince to fuck off when he comes down on the Brujah that decided he's an anarch.<br /> Caitiff don't have anyone with a similar weakness to bond over, other than how everyone knows it and hates them for it. they don't even share the same discipline spreads, so they'll have little in common.<br /> <br /> I think the only exception to this rule are the <b>Followers of Set</b>, because there's no reason to support eachother over light sensitivity and yet they so rarely go Anarch (don't go there). They do, however, make up for it by being a Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T05:56:25-07:00","id":1460517,"title":"","content":"My general view of the Anarchs is the fact that you don't actually have to choose motivations for the majority of them and that their &quot;membership&quot; in the Movement isn't necessarily going to be something that is solely driven by one factor or another.<br /> <br /> <b>Reasons to be an Anarch</b><br /> <br /> 1. A vampire that has successfully pissed off the Prince is going to have to either leave town or seek allies against persecution. This is basically what drives the Fledgling in LA by Night since they were &quot;born a crime.&quot;<br /> 2. A vampire might actually join the Anarchs for power. Gordon Keaton is a yuppie professional but he was Embraced as a Caitiff so the best way to become influential is to be an Anarch.<br /> 3. A vampire might be an Anarch simply because the vampires he hangs out about and likes are Anarchs themselves. If you're not of the Elysium crowd, you might well prefer to have Gengis or Anita Wainwright. Which makes you an Anarch by default.<br /> 4. The fact that plenty of vampires join the Anarchs because they hate an Elder or powerful Kindred. Allicia joined the Anarchs despite being a Toreador because she hated Modius and helped her overthrow them.<br /> 5. Being Embraced into the Movement. If you're Smiling Jack's childe, you're not really going to be welcome at Camarilla shindigs. Especially if they didn't get any Prince's permission.<br /> 6. Some Princes are going to treat you like one just for your lineage if you're Caitiff, an orphan, or Thin Blood.<br /> 7. Some Kindred will genuinely just hate the fact they can be killed at any time for crimes that are of dubious merit.<br /> 8. Being an Anarch can actually be financially and politically useful. Bizarrely, if you have a reputation as a outsider and legbreaker then some Elders and people will be interested in using you as a weapon.<br /> 9. Getting swept up in the mortal movements of the day like the French Revolution or Occupy Wallstreet can also result in you wanting to go against the current Camarilla system.<br /> 10. People opposed to the current Prince or structure may be Anarchs until it is settled down. You're &quot;Anarchs&quot; until you overthrow the Prince and are now the new establishment.<br /> <br /> None of which are actually contradictory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the only exception to this rule are the Followers of Set, because there's no reason to support eachother over light sensitivity and yet they so rarely go Anarch (don't go there). They do, however, make up for it by being a Cult. </div> </div> </div>Eh, it depends on how you define Anarch. I imagine Anarch domains are perfect places for Followers of Set seeking disenfranchised young lost souls and peddling vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T06:26:16-07:00","id":1460521,"title":"","content":"The main thing I do with Anarchs is stress the overcrowding/stretched resources and that means the first thing that has to go is the not-so-sacred 1:100k ratio. It\u2019s too low for there to ever be a need for Anarchs because that\u2019s basically one person in an entire typical midwestern city like I live in.<br /> <br /> Do you know how hard it would be to track down one person in that if you didn\u2019t even know who you were looking for? I\u2019ve lived here for decades and I assure you I\u2019ve never met more than a bare fraction of them; 5% if I were being generous. Maybe 25% if you counted attending the same event as \u201cmeeting.\u201d And I still wouldn\u2019t know that this one particular person I don\u2019t know of is, let\u2019s say an orthodontist, from having attended the same event with them.<br /> <br /> Basically, 1:100k is too low for Anarchs to exist. It\u2019s just way too easy to just \u201cNope\u201d out of vampire society and live in the background noise of being a second in 100k vampire where unless you colossally fuck up you\u2019re never likely to be noticed.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also too low for all but the largest metro areas to have more than a token Camarilla organization to rebel against. At 1:100k just filling the bureaucracy spots to make it feel like a true organization and not an after school club for mean girls takes a metro population of 2.3 million (Prince, Sheriff, a couple Hounds, Scourge, Senechal, Herald, Harpy, Keeper of Elysium, a full Primogen and their Whips) and that\u2019s with no one to actually boss around.<br /> <br /> Cut positions and make it more informal so there\u2019s someone to boss around and there\u2019s even less of a need to rebel because the organization that is there doesn\u2019t have the manpower to keep other vamps from noping out and disappearing into the masses.<br /> <br /> So, for real Anarchs to make sense you need to explode the ratio; 1:10,000 or even 1:3000; so the resources are tight enough relative to the risk of discovery for their to be haves and have-nots and a fully vested group of elites playing favorites. Now there\u2019s something to rebel against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T07:23:57-07:00","id":1460525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460521#post1460521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing I do with Anarchs is stress the overcrowding/stretched resources and that means the first thing that has to go is the not-so-sacred 1:100k ratio. It\u2019s too low for there to ever be a need for Anarchs because that\u2019s basically one person in an entire typical midwestern city like I live in.<br /> <br /> Do you know how hard it would be to track down one person in that if you didn\u2019t even know who you were looking for? I\u2019ve lived here for decades and I assure you I\u2019ve never met more than a bare fraction of them; 5% if I were being generous. Maybe 25% if you counted attending the same event as \u201cmeeting.\u201d And I still wouldn\u2019t know that this one particular person I don\u2019t know of is, let\u2019s say an orthodontist, from having attended the same event with them.<br /> <br /> Basically, 1:100k is too low for Anarchs to exist. It\u2019s just way too easy to just \u201cNope\u201d out of vampire society and live in the background noise of being a second in 100k vampire where unless you colossally fuck up you\u2019re never likely to be noticed.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also too low for all but the largest metro areas to have more than a token Camarilla organization to rebel against. At 1:100k just filling the bureaucracy spots to make it feel like a true organization and not an after school club for mean girls takes a metro population of 2.3 million (Prince, Sheriff, a couple Hounds, Scourge, Senechal, Herald, Harpy, Keeper of Elysium, a full Primogen and their Whips) and that\u2019s with no one to actually boss around.<br /> <br /> Cut positions and make it more informal so there\u2019s someone to boss around and there\u2019s even less of a need to rebel because the organization that is there doesn\u2019t have the manpower to keep other vamps from noping out and disappearing into the masses.<br /> <br /> So, for real Anarchs to make sense you need to explode the ratio; 1:10,000 or even 1:3000; so the resources are tight enough relative to the risk of discovery for their to be haves and have-nots and a fully vested group of elites playing favorites. Now there\u2019s something to rebel against.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe 1:100K is actually the &quot;safe&quot; number of vampires to be in an area without detection. I believe for exactly the reasons you describe.<br /> <br /> How overpopulated vampiredom is an interesting question.<br /> <br /> Also affected by how many other supernaturals are in your World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Still, I think you underestimate how much vampires are likely to feud. Even if the numbers are closer to a high school than a nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T07:53:19-07:00","id":1460531,"title":"","content":"While naturally different circumstances call for different peculiarities, this is the rub of how I handle my Anarchs:<br /> <br /> First of all \u2018Anarch\u2019 is a pejorative exonym and refers to a broad swath of ideologies which are only loosely associated and only rarely affiliated. Historically it was applied by elders and brood patriarchs (patriarch here being gender neutral) to describe vampires who rejected the dictates of their elders and \u201cbetters\u201d. For most of settled agrarianate history there was little ideological coherence amongst Anarchs and often they simply elevated one of their own to the position of patriarch or claimed a new domain if they were successful before returning to the status quo. There are exceptions to this but that\u2019s the broad rule<br /> <br /> The rise of ideologically coherent anarchs is new to the modern era (although comparisons can be made to the primitive republics and ideological communes which did begin in the Classical Age). Amongst these Anarchs, only some are actually followers of the political philosophy of Anarchism, and while those who aren\u2019t may accept the title of \u2018anarch\u2019 or reject it in their own discourse, it\u2019s often used as a catch-all to describe all vampires who have: rejected clan patriarchs, rejected the traditional sects, are not dedicated autarkis (although the Anarchs do have some overlap with Autarkis).<br /> <br /> Anarchs come in basically every political stripe that isn\u2019t already accounted for by the militant theocracy of the Sabbat or the neofuedal confederation of the Camarilla. Contemporary Anarchs are associated particularly with left-wing ideologies such as Anarchism, Socialism, and Communism but this is not a hard and fast rule. One will also find Fascists and the like amongst the ranks of Anarchs. The modern era also famously saw the rise of Anarchs who professed the ideals of Liberalism, Democracy, and Republicanism; thus rejecting the aristocratic legacy of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> While political ideologies translate differently to vampires than they do to mortal humans, the ideological drive they provide can give motivation to vampires to resist the status quo of the sects.<br /> <br /> Now Anarchs come on a spectrum. You have rebellious and unruly youths who are Anarchs simply because they dislike the stuffy edicts of Elysium and these will either assimilate or become more radicalized with time. You have autarkis who just want to be left alone. You have cynics who use the title of anarch simply to rally a dissatisfied base for the purpose of claiming power themselves. You have the loyal opposition who operate within their systems but want to use the Anarchs as lever of power to effect reform. You have mercenaries who use the title of Anarchs to be soldiers of fortune. You also have genuine ideologues of every stripe: soldiers, visionaries, theorists, propagandists, revolutionaries, prophets, and so much more. People truly dedicated to their ideals, whatever they are, willing to kill and die to see them realized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T08:15:14-07:00","id":1460533,"title":"","content":"Obligatory Requiem player's jab : like always failing Carthians. <br /> <br /> More realistically, the Anarchs have to have some successes and be more than mere rabble rousers and disgrunted low-lives to be considered a potential threat to the Camarilla. They have to have enough on an appeal globaly, or at least regionally, for them to be seen as dangerous to the Camarilla's way of life.<br /> <br /> If every attempt at an Anarch free city turns into riots, blood hunts and general madness even faster than a Sabbat's stronghold does, then this sect is simply unable to sustain itself. That it has does so for centuries means that it should be able to have perfectly viable cities able to fend off Cam and Sabbat incursions. Perhaps by resorting to a sort of &quot;citizen's militia&quot; and &quot;will of the people&quot; rethoric and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T09:55:33-07:00","id":1460549,"title":"","content":"I think the Anarchs must be an interesting &quot;faction&quot; for players, much like how <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a> described. But I really avoid making them anything resembling a sect.<br /> <br /> There are two broad ways to define Anarchs. Either they are actual Anarchists or they are an umbrella term. If they are actual Anarchists, they inherently lack enough organization to offer the semblance of a sect. They are independent agents that oppose any formal power structure and only organize around mutual agreement. Any charismatic individual can garner some personal power among them, and you can get people to really work together in some projects, but no greater structure can form.<br /> <br /> Being an Umbrella term, you have a too fractured bunch to deal with. They are Anarchs in the sense that they recognize a system and oppose it, but nothing else. This kind of Anarch works well as a catch-all term for disgruntled Kindred inside a clearly defined domain, or as a specific small group that have a more cohesive identity. If an Anarch Baron achieves to secure a city out of Camarilla's hands, this Baron either creates an alternative structure that works only in their domain (be it just a copy of Camarilla or not), or keeps order through personal power alone, be it through charisma, fear or both. This can be a powerful Kindred and even a powerful domain, but there is no larger structure to support it. I dare to say that many Kindred that achieve such position will actually petition to be recognized as Prince by Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the disgruntled kindred flesh out vampiric population more than anything else. On most domains it is more like a political party, where the Anarchs are the ones opposed to the current <i>status quo</i> in the city, although not necessarily by the Camarilla as a structure. At this level, their personal differences matter less and they can work as a group. They can even have support from other Anarch groups in other cities, similarly to how opposition to any ruler can work together to a common goal and even display some political unity despite actually having disparaging political views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T10:25:52-07:00","id":1460553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460525#post1460525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe 1:100K is actually the &amp;quot;safe&amp;quot; number of vampires to be in an area without detection. I believe for exactly the reasons you describe.<br /> <br /> How overpopulated vampiredom is an interesting question.<br /> <br /> Also affected by how many other supernaturals are in your World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Still, I think you underestimate how much vampires are likely to feud. Even if the numbers are closer to a high school than a nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to find another vampire in order to feud with them. I think an excellent example of this is actually a social group we\u2019re all quite familiar with given the forum; tabletop role players.<br /> <br /> I know dozens of them in my area (again a midwestern city with about the population to support one vampire af the idealized level); which is only a fraction of the total; and if not for the couple of FLGS and a Meetup group, I\u2019d never have been aware of even them.<br /> <br /> If I started my own group from newbies (i.e. sired some fledglings) and played only with them, the larger gamer community wouldn\u2019t even know they existed.<br /> <br /> Now, gamers are more insular than vampires who need to procure a stable blood supply without arousing suspicion, but the ratio is also much bigger too... on the order of 1:1000 or more and we\u2019d still completely miss each other if we weren\u2019t actively seeking each other out.<br /> <br /> Similarly, even in this city of 100k, there are easily a dozen plus night clubs and bars that singles hit to hook up almost nightly.* A vampire can only be in one place at a time so that\u2019s a dozen or more small but separate hunting grounds just in a population of 100k people using only the most stereotypical method. If you had just two vampires in the entire community (twice the \u201csafe\u201d ratio) there\u2019s zero pressure to fight... you see the other vampire already at that nightclub and go to one of the other eleven. The first vampire would literally need to be wanting to pick a fight for their to be a conflict.<br /> <br /> And even if they DO want to pick a fight, predators rarely fight to the death unless there is a desperate shortage of resources, it\u2019s just not a good survival strategy; you don\u2019t provoke a fight with a fellow predator unless you have to. Instead one proves their superiority and the other avoids them and goes elsewhere if they turn up... and again, there\u2019s no shortage of hunting grounds at even 2:100k.<br /> <br /> Basically, you need a 12:100k ratio just to get 1 vampire per prime feeding spot and a 13:100k ratio before someone\u2019s really going to want to compete for a prime spot. And that\u2019s just the prime spots... throw in the men\u2019s and women\u2019s homeless shelters, the Red Cross center, hospitals, outside of 24/7 shopping locations, etc. and you could easily double that... and this in a small city where just about everything shuts down at 9pm vs. the all night bustle of a larger city.<br /> <br /> Which is why I say you really need ratios in the 1:10k or higher range before enough of the easy hunting grounds are taken for there to be a reason to start problems over access to them. That or a bunch of really careless vampires who overfeed and start leaving bodies on a regular basis... which is also unlikely to happen if there\u2019s enough food to go around since it\u2019s mostly the hungry vampires who lose control and have a drained body on their hands.**<br /> <br /> Sure, the Camarilla/Mean Girls\u2019 Society doesn\u2019t need an excuse to plot against each other and would do so regardless the ratio, but that\u2019s not the same thing as having an Anarch movement. For that you need enough have \u201cnots\u201d to make the dictates of the \u201chaves\u201d feel like an unreasonable burden instead of something you can just ignore.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s also where you\u2019d expect the \u201chaves\u201d to start getting exclusive rather than inclusive and start persecuting various outgroups to protect what they see as theirs. Until there\u2019s actually the potential for a shortage, there\u2019s little need to rigorously enforce access to the resource and probably not enough manpower to actually police access to something as fluid as human activity.<br /> <br /> Going back to the two vampires and a dozen nightclubs; the dominant vampire would need at least 11 assistants informed of who specifically to look for to cover the other locations before they could reasonably stop the lesser vampire from getting a meal in one of the others... and more to keep the lesser out of the hospitals, the homeless shelters, the jail, the parks, the truck stops, etc. The logistics just aren\u2019t there for policing access to such a massive population relative to a lone vampire.<br /> <br /> 1:100k is the ticket to a quiet life of easy hunting for everyone involved; but this is the World of Darkness so the idea that undead existence should be that idyllic should be thrown out on its ear in the name of having a setting with actual dramatic tension and conflicts.<br /> <br /> My current campaign is using 1:10k and even it feels a bit on the idyllic side; there\u2019s just too many places to hunt even in clusters of 10k humans for there to be much to fight over. The Anarchs are less Anarchs as they are the suburban bar vampires; ones who\u2019s available hunting grounds are basically eating at McDonald\u2019s compared to the elite\u2019s 4-5 star dining options. You could gripe about the quality, but that\u2019s not usually enough to get into fights to the death over and not enough for the Prince to feel much pressure to persecute anyone for stepping outside their lanes. You\u2019d need a serious spark to set off any sort of powder keg of conflict there (my PCs are thankfully cooperating there as one of them is looking to overthrow the Prince as revenge for a slight the Prince may not have even been involved in... the sheer number of contenders if they were to succeed would probably lead to the city exploding into something like last summer\u2019s riots as various players activate their assets against each other... and even that would only peripherally involve actual Anarchs; mostly as foot soldiers made promises by whichever factions they throw in with).<br /> <br /> * one thing that made the population issue readily apparent was when my group moved to Discord due to Covid and someone started putting together a Google Earth project marking key territories and sites for the city... and we started seeing all the local bars and nightclubs and other prime hunting grounds dotting the city. It really makes the 1:100k number feel like it was pulled out of the ether by a bunch of people who\u2019d never lived in a big city (even a sleepy midwestern one like mine) and explored it\u2019s nightlife and got all their ideas from reading about city life in the 90\u2019s from books printed in the 80\u2019s.<br /> <br /> ** and since guilt over draining someone is one of the bigger reasons for an impulsive unsanctioned Embrace, it\u2019s a problem that will actually escalate the overpopulation crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T10:30:48-07:00","id":1460554,"title":"","content":"A couple of points:<br /> <br /> 1. In the World of Darkness, it is very likely the term &quot;Anarch&quot; among vampires isn't a reference to anarchism as a political philosophy. The Anarchist political philosophy was a product of the 18th century but vampire Anarchs referred to as Anarchs have existed since the 12th century (600 years earlier). Vampire Anarchs is thus likely to be a reference to &quot;The Anarchy&quot; of England in all likelihood (1135 to 1153) during the Civil War of King Stephen and Empress Matilda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/BattleOf_Lincoln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\"> The Anarchy - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The term &quot;Anarch&quot; is thus a pejorative of vampires referring to the fact that individual vampires were revolting against the natural order of their Elders and a breakdown of formal vampire society. It is something that said revoltees would take as a badge of honor symbolizing their defiance against the Law of Caine.<br /> <br /> 2. Anarchs don't have to be a traditional nation state to win against the Camarilla. They also don't have to have much in the way of organization or even shared ideals to work together. The relatively small numbers of vampires and their secrecy means that really they just need to share a limited amount of resources across global lines (which is a lot easier in the Modern Era) to work against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As we've seen with Marcus Vitel, Emperor of Washington D.C., you might even have an incredibly despotic Lasombra Methuselah as a &quot;Anarch&quot; as long as he's paying for the revolution elsewhere. Certainly, the Soviet Union sponsored a lot of revolutions elsewhere and Anarchs Unbound retconned the Brujah Council to be financing Anarchs far and abroad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-20-2021, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T10:43:36-07:00","id":1460556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460553#post1460553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to find another vampire in order to feud with them. I think an excellent example of this is actually a social group we\u2019re all quite familiar with given the forum; tabletop role players.<br /> <br /> I know dozens of them in my area (again a midwestern city with about the population to support one vampire af the idealized level); which is only a fraction of the total; and if not for the couple of FLGS and a Meetup group, I\u2019d never have been aware of even them.<br /> <br /> If I started my own group from newbies (i.e. sired some fledglings) and played only with them, the larger gamer community wouldn\u2019t even know they existed.<br /> <br /> Now, gamers are more insular than vampires who need to procure a stable blood supply without arousing suspicion, but the ratio is also much bigger too... on the order of 1:1000 or more and we\u2019d still completely miss each other if we weren\u2019t actively seeking each other out.<br /> <br /> Similarly, even in this city of 100k, there are easily a dozen plus night clubs and bars that singles hit to hook up almost nightly.* A vampire can only be in one place at a time so that\u2019s a dozen or more small but separate hunting grounds just in a population of 100k people using only the most stereotypical method. If you had just two vampires in the entire community (twice the \u201csafe\u201d ratio) there\u2019s zero pressure to fight... you see the other vampire already at that nightclub and go to one of the other eleven. The first vampire would literally need to be wanting to pick a fight for their to be a conflict.<br /> <br /> And even if they DO want to pick a fight, predators rarely fight to the death unless there is a desperate shortage of resources, it\u2019s just not a good survival strategy; you don\u2019t provoke a fight with a fellow predator unless you have to. Instead one proves their superiority and the other avoids them and goes elsewhere if they turn up... and again, there\u2019s no shortage of hunting grounds at even 2:100k.<br /> <br /> Basically, you need a 12:100k ratio just to get 1 vampire per prime feeding spot and a 13:100k ratio before someone\u2019s really going to want to compete for a prime spot. And that\u2019s just the prime spots... throw in the men\u2019s and women\u2019s homeless shelters, the Red Cross center, hospitals, outside of 24/7 shopping locations, etc. and you could easily double that... and this in a small city where just about everything shuts down at 9pm vs. the all night bustle of a larger city.<br /> <br /> Which is why I say you really need ratios in the 1:10k or higher range before enough of the easy hunting grounds are taken for there to be a reason to start problems over access to them. That or a bunch of really careless vampires who overfeed and start leaving bodies on a regular basis... which is also unlikely to happen if there\u2019s enough food to go around since it\u2019s mostly the hungry vampires who lose control and have a drained body on their hands.**<br /> <br /> Sure, the Camarilla/Mean Girls\u2019 Society doesn\u2019t need an excuse to plot against each other and would do so regardless the ratio, but that\u2019s not the same thing as having an Anarch movement. For that you need enough have \u201cnots\u201d to make the dictates of the \u201chaves\u201d feel like an unreasonable burden instead of something you can just ignore.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s also where you\u2019d expect the \u201chaves\u201d to start getting exclusive rather than inclusive and start persecuting various outgroups to protect what they see as theirs. Until there\u2019s actually the potential for a shortage, there\u2019s little need to rigorously enforce access to the resource and probably not enough manpower to actually police access to something as fluid as human activity.<br /> <br /> Going back to the two vampires and a dozen nightclubs; the dominant vampire would need at least 11 assistants informed of who specifically to look for to cover the other locations before they could reasonably stop the lesser vampire from getting a meal in one of the others... and more to keep the lesser out of the hospitals, the homeless shelters, the jail, the parks, the truck stops, etc. The logistics just aren\u2019t there for policing access to such a massive population relative to a lone vampire.<br /> <br /> 1:100k is the ticket to a quiet life of easy hunting for everyone involved; but this is the World of Darkness so the idea that undead existence should be that idyllic should be thrown out on its ear in the name of having a setting with actual dramatic tension and conflicts.<br /> <br /> My current campaign is using 1:10k and even it feels a bit on the idyllic side; there\u2019s just too many places to hunt even in clusters of 10k humans for there to be much to fight over. The Anarchs are less Anarchs as they are the suburban bar vampires; ones who\u2019s available hunting grounds are basically eating at McDonald\u2019s compared to the elite\u2019s 4-5 star dining options. You could gripe about the quality, but that\u2019s not usually enough to get into fights to the death over and not enough for the Prince to feel much pressure to persecute anyone for stepping outside their lanes. You\u2019d need a serious spark to set off any sort of powder keg of conflict there (my PCs are thankfully cooperating there as one of them is looking to overthrow the Prince as revenge for a slight the Prince may not have even been involved in... the sheer number of contenders if they were to succeed would probably lead to the city exploding into something like last summer\u2019s riots as various players activate their assets against each other... and even that would only peripherally involve actual Anarchs; mostly as foot soldiers made promises by whichever factions they throw in with).<br /> <br /> * one thing that made the population issue readily apparent was when my group moved to Discord due to Covid and someone started putting together a Google Earth project marking key territories and sites for the city... and we started seeing all the local bars and nightclubs and other prime hunting grounds dotting the city. It really makes the 1:100k number feel like it was pulled out of the ether by a bunch of people who\u2019d never lived in a big city (even a sleepy midwestern one like mine) and explored it\u2019s nightlife and got all their ideas from reading about city life in the 90\u2019s from books printed in the 80\u2019s.<br /> <br /> ** and since guilt over draining someone is one of the bigger reasons for an impulsive unsanctioned Embrace, it\u2019s a problem that will actually escalate the overpopulation crisis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think those numbers don't work at all but I'm someone who has put an inordinant amount of thought into my silly vampire game as well as the idea that vampires are people who have a lot of preferences. Feel free to disagree and I welcome your insights into this matter but this is what I have thought about vampire competition for resources.<br /> <br /> 1. Assuming 1 Blood Point equals a pint of blood, drinking from the same person every night will kill them. So you must drink from multiple vessels without them ever being drank from regularly.<br /> <br /> 2. 1:10000 sounds like its perfectly idyllic except for the fact that vampires are not going to be feeding evenly.<br /> <br /> 3. Vampires are going to want to avoid feeding from the sick and dying or geriatric unless they are on a Path and able to stomach regularly killing their victims (which is why the Giovanni never have a problem feeding in my games).<br /> <br /> 4. Vampires as a general rule do not feed off of children, which eliminates another huge chunk of the populace.<br /> <br /> 5. Vampires generally prefer to feed from easy targets which means that clubs, bars, homeless, and prostitutes are an obvious group.<br /> <br /> 6. Vampires generally prefer to feed on the healthy within the 20s to 40s range.<br /> <br /> 7. Vampires by nature are social animals and do want to associate with their own kind because they require it as a sense of normalcy.<br /> <br /> 8. Vampires who use their Disciplines in any shape or form is going to require far more than to feed on 30 separate people per month. Which is only if they are<br /> doing their best not to &quot;double dip&quot; on the same vessels and do permanent lasting harm.<br /> <br /> 9. Barring the use of Mental Disciplines, actually getting these 30 separate people into positions to be fed on is a lot harder than it sounds.<br /> <br /> 10. Vampires prefer to feed on the physically attractive too because it's that sort of game.<br /> <br /> 11. Vampires do not only compete for blood within their hunting domains. They also compete for resources such as wealth, status, social position, and power.<br /> <br /> 12. There are other supernaturals to worry about in a World of Darkness if you make a large enough stink such as werewolves and hunters.<br /> <br /> 13. Most vampires congregate in Big Cities since rarely does a vampire want to be the only vampire in Nowheresville, IL even if it gives him access to, say<br /> 30K people by his lonesome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T11:20:02-07:00","id":1460558,"title":"","content":"The thing often forgot is that modern Cities are really, really big. Even if we talk about dense cities and forget the farcical ponzi schemes of north american city planning (constantly building suburbs to pay for the repair of other suburbs) it's very likely that several vampires can occupy a city for centuries and not know about each other, depending on the type of vampire that is: The Typical Toreador will flock to the club and red light district for feeding, and in small cities there's generally only one of those, but smaller pubs will dot the city and most clans can Obfuscate or Dominate and thus attach themselves to an institution or make a good go of feeding from the homeless. <br /> <br /> Speaking of farcical north american city planning (Houston, we have a problem, I can't fucking walk anywhere, you're a giant fucking parking lot) That's an environment that's going to breed Anarchs. Too decentralized, too much disparity in good feeding grounds, the Car reliance actually hurts elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T11:25:29-07:00","id":1460560,"title":"","content":"I have a long post, so to start with, I'll just say that my approach is largely a 1st edition, early 2nd edition, V20 combination. That is the short answer, the long answer follows regarding the politics of the Anarch movement.<br /> <br /> First let's talk about how vampires have wealth:<br /> <br /> Imagine a hungry man is walking across the country side. He sees a bunch of sheep grazing on the grass. They don't even run away, he can walk right up to them and kill them without any struggle. He sees edible plants growing in the field, arranged in neat little rows so he can just go and eat to his heart's content. It seems like this man, with little to no work, can have all of the food he wants. But, the truth is that he can't because all of this food belongs to other people who have spent years cultivating their land and building up their flocks. If he tries to take their stuff, he's in for some trouble.<br /> <br /> So the world of the rich and powerful must seem to a new vampire with the ability to blood bind people and a few points of Dominate and/or Presence. The world seems to be your oyster - go to the mayor and make him your servant, make the local billionaire businessman your servant too. Make the chief of police your ghoul so that you can get away with crimes. As with the hungry man above, just walk through the garden and eat to your heart's content.<br /> <br /> BUT - other vampires exist too and they have already plucked or claimed the low hanging fruit. The elders are invested in these humans with wealth and power, they are invested in the businesses and institutions that get things done in a city. You can't very well go along and claim them as your own any more than you can walk into a grocery store and start eating food off the shelves.<br /> <br /> Vampires are social and economic parasites as much as they are literal blood drinkers. The humans can do the day to day chores of running businesses and they can learn all about economic models and marketing or how to day trade - but which ever mortals end up making money are going to be under the direct or indirect sway of some elder vampire somewhere. Becoming a rich vampire has less to do with being a businessman or even a domitor yourself and more to do with playing the political game against other vampires to get your own piece of a pie that has been baked and sliced long before you started playing the game.<br /> <br /> So this is the world that a young vampire finds itself in. A world of seemingly unlimited riches, but its all tightly controlled and to get a cut you must serve creatures that could potentially live forever. Of course, most older vampires are going to let neonates, especially their own childer, get a big enough piece of the pie to stay loyal and contented, a reward for good service.<br /> <br /> That opens up an extremely important question: <b>why does a vampire embrace a childe?</b> To be a companion, a slave, a servant, a lover, a warrior, a research assistant, a bodyguard, an heir, a extra vote in the political arena, for fun? All of the above. Embraces are tightly controlled in the Camarilla and usually the vampire doing so had to the earn that right, do a favor for the prince, or maybe just has a fortunate opportunity. In any case, most vampires of moderate or greater age are going to want something from their childer and wont take kindly to them running off and saying that they don't like<i> the man</i>. So childer are going to selected for obedience and/or alliance, so if that childe opposes the sire, they will be punished severely or perhaps killed. A childe opposing the sire is a disaster, because it was a big investment that didn't pay off and that wise sires are going to try to prevent. So then where do Anarchs come from?<br /> <br /> The simplest explanation is the the sire is an Anarch and so the childe is an Anarch too. Ironically the childe becomes an Anarch in obedience to the sire. In the scenario, the Anarchs are acting like a political more than a movement of the youth against the old. We have Anarch elders served by Anarch ancilla, served by Anarch neonates - opposed to Camarilla establishment elders, establishment ancilla, and establishment neonates. The Anarch faction may have rhetoric about rights and freedoms for the young, but the political struggle is more about which faction gets the bigger pieces of the above pie - both factions have elders at the top and neonates at the bottom.<br /> <br /> Another source of Anarchs might be vampires that aren't that young, but who are ancilla. Brand new vampires are probably too much in awe of their new powers and too terrified of mysterious elders to want to rock the boat. Give the vampires a bit of time though and having mind controlled human slaves or super strength starts to get boring, they can see the pie in its totality and realize that they want a bigger piece of the pie. Vampires of this age have more independence from their sires and can't just be killed like an unreleased childe. They also have enough power to not unlive in terror of elders or Camarilla authorities. In many of these cases, maybe the vampire's sire or other authorities have died, gone into torpor, left the city, or otherwise are no longer in the picture. Once a vampire of intermediate age gets actual independence, then they will realize that they may be independent but don't have much individual power. So they team up with other young to moderate aged independent vampires to fight for their own power against more established elders.<br /> <br /> This time is a vampire's life, when they start to actually gain some measure of independence and power, is probably regarded as dangerous to the elders. Many vampires of this age probably don't become Anarchs because their drive for power is probably redirected, not at the elders but somewhere else. Maybe such an ancilla identifies with their Clan and gains power within the framework of their Clan and at the expense of rival Clans. As many socialists might say, the rich elites divide the working class based on ethnicity so that they fight each other. Clan divisions are kind of like that, though whether or not vampires should unite based on age or based on Clan is a bit subjective. Alternatively, the ancilla might ally with elders and become valuable to them, increasing power by being useful to other vampires of power. Alternatively, the vampire might strike off to a new place where there are more opportunities, so could become an elder, or perhaps an Anarch, in some distant city.<br /> <br /> In very tightly controlled cities, there would likely be no Anarchs or the Anarchs there would just be one faction ruled by its own elders, as I mentioned above. In such a city, embraces are tightly controlled and young vampires are made to realize that disobedience could cute short their immortality. In more chaotic regions, embraces might happen far more frequently and childer may become independent far sooner, maybe even immediately. In such a city, a true Anarch movement can quickly grow to power, though likely still under the control of older vampires. This kind of situation is probably what made California possible.<br /> <br /> I see the Anarch movement as something that happens within the Camarilla, and very seldom an independent political. In many cases Anarchs are labeled such not by themselves but by the elders who derisively label young vampires as Anarchs when they organize to advocate for more rights or powers for young vampires. Like in 1st edition V:tM, I see the Elder vs Anarch conflict as the central political conflict in the setting, not Camarilla vs Sabbat, vampires vs werewolves, or anything like that. Well, Clan versus Clan might sometimes compete with that, or humanity versus beast. A high percentage of cities are going to have Anarchs or something like them, though very often its less a movement that actually advances the rights of young vampires, and more an opposition party that just empowers a different set of elders. These Anarch elders might be worse that the establishment ones in many ways, since they are demagogues who gain power by telling younger vampires that they deserve just as much power as vampires who have spent centuries gaining wisdom and earning power, and they wont have that power anyway because they will just be serving a different set of elders.<br /> <br /> Anarchs very seldom drive the Camarilla from a city, usually they don't even want that. They want varying degrees of greater rights and powers for young vampires or merely their own faction, and very often they succeed at this by getting the prince to change certain policies or even having a prince who is affiliated with the Anarchs - in which case we might ironically have a dissident faction within the city that seeks more traditional elder lead politics. In either case, it is still a Camarilla city and the Anarchs succeed within the context of Camarilla law rather than completely rejecting it: which would seriously increase the dangers since they have then declared war on the Inner Circle and Justicars and will probably be crushed.<br /> <br /> Depending on the local prince and dominant elders, even those Anarch elders might actually represent an increase in freedom, resources, or some other desirable policy.<br /> <br /> Brujah elders tend to attract the support of ancilla (and maybe neonates) by promising them a bigger piece of the pie at the expense of the elders. The Ventrue elders tend to attract the support of ancilla (and maybe neonates) by telling them the benefits of cooperating with the elders and the virtues of patience. Other Clans fall somewhere along that spectrum, or go in a perpendicular direction of advocating Clan loyalty above age loyalty - like Tremere or Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Well, that is enough rambling for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 09-20-2021, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T11:37:09-07:00","id":1460561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460558#post1460558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing often forgot is that modern Cities are really, really big. Even if we talk about dense cities and forget the farcical ponzi schemes of north american city planning (constantly building suburbs to pay for the repair of other suburbs) it's very likely that several vampires can occupy a city for centuries and not know about each other, depending on the type of vampire that is: The Typical Toreador will flock to the club and red light district for feeding, and in small cities there's generally only one of those, but smaller pubs will dot the city and most clans can Obfuscate or Dominate and thus attach themselves to an institution or make a good go of feeding from the homeless.<br /> <br /> Speaking of farcical north american city planning (Houston, we have a problem, I can't fucking walk anywhere, you're a giant fucking parking lot) That's an environment that's going to breed Anarchs. Too decentralized, too much disparity in good feeding grounds, the Car reliance actually hurts elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which runs into the fact that vampires don't WANT to avoid each other generally. They actively seek each other out and if they were completely alone in a city, they'd quickly Embrace new vampires to fill it up.<br /> <br /> Mind you, you're not wrong. I think the most hilarious and yet accurate idea of CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5TH EDITION is the revelation there were apparently an additional 20-40 vampires in the gay and trans community and an entire Lilith-worshiping Caitiff empire that Lodin's brood did not know about.<br /> <br /> And then its like, &quot;Who the hell are these guys?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T12:01:58-07:00","id":1460562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460556#post1460556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think those numbers don't work at all but I'm someone who has put an inordinant amount of thought into my silly vampire game as well as the idea that vampires are people who have a lot of preferences. Feel free to disagree and I welcome your insights into this matter but this is what I have thought about vampire competition for resources.<br /> <br /> 1. Assuming 1 Blood Point equals a pint of blood, drinking from the same person every night will kill them. So you must drink from multiple vessels without them ever being drank from regularly.<br /> <br /> 2. 1:10000 sounds like its perfectly idyllic except for the fact that vampires are not going to be feeding evenly.<br /> <br /> 3. Vampires are going to want to avoid feeding from the sick and dying or geriatric unless they are on a Path and able to stomach regularly killing their victims (which is why the Giovanni never have a problem feeding in my games).<br /> <br /> 4. Vampires as a general rule do not feed off of children, which eliminates another huge chunk of the populace.<br /> <br /> 5. Vampires generally prefer to feed from easy targets which means that clubs, bars, homeless, and prostitutes are an obvious group.<br /> <br /> 6. Vampires generally prefer to feed on the healthy within the 20s to 40s range.<br /> <br /> 7. Vampires by nature are social animals and do want to associate with their own kind because they require it as a sense of normalcy.<br /> <br /> 8. Vampires who use their Disciplines in any shape or form is going to require far more than to feed on 30 separate people per month. Which is only if they are<br /> doing their best not to &quot;double dip&quot; on the same vessels and do permanent lasting harm.<br /> <br /> 9. Barring the use of Mental Disciplines, actually getting these 30 separate people into positions to be fed on is a lot harder than it sounds.<br /> <br /> 10. Vampires prefer to feed on the physically attractive too because it's that sort of game.<br /> <br /> 11. Vampires do not only compete for blood within their hunting domains. They also compete for resources such as wealth, status, social position, and power.<br /> <br /> 12. There are other supernaturals to worry about in a World of Darkness if you make a large enough stink such as werewolves and hunters.<br /> <br /> 13. Most vampires congregate in Big Cities since rarely does a vampire want to be the only vampire in Nowheresville, IL even if it gives him access to, say<br /> 30K people by his lonesome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>None of those numbers support anything close to needing a 1:100k ratio inside a city.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the basics... one vampire feeding on 2 BP/night at the same rate as the Red Cross indicates is safe to donate a &quot;Double Red&quot; (2 pints); once every 16 weeks; is <b>112</b> individuals. This is basically a 1 BP/night plus periodic excess use to the tune of 365 extra blood points per year.<br /> <br /> Now let's see what it would take to get there.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the basics... let's limit ourselves to just the population between According to the <a href=\"https://www.census.gov/data/tables/2019/demo/age-and-sex/2019-age-sex-composition.html\" target=\"_blank\">US Census</a> in the United States the population between the ages of 21-44 is 31.9%. So, out of 100k individuals the vampiric preference in #6 above is a population of <b>31,900</b> individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, lets throw out the percentage who are married, since they're far less likely to be in the establishments a vampire would be hunting at at the hours a vampire is looking for a meal. Again per the census that ranges from 31.5% married in the 25-29 age group, to 66% in the 40-45 age group. Let's use the 66% just because it will cut down the population the most... so of the 31,900 people you've got at least <b>10,846</b> people who are single and between the ages of 21-44.<br /> <br /> Let's further take another 90% off that just for all the other potential factors; too sick, too ugly, incompatible work schedule, shut-ins, etc. This is an extreme, just as using the highest marriage rate above to exclude potential targets was... but its to prove the point. Having access to just 10% of the single 21-44 year olds in a population of 100k still leaves you with <b>1085</b> people... and a single vampire needs only 112 to obtain 2 BP/day without endangering those they're feeding from. If you did a new target every night it would take you nearly three years to get through that 10%.<br /> <br /> And that's being extremely conservative. A more likely number is probably 3-5000+ available happy meals on legs per 100k of the human population and more than enough to support 10-12 vampires per 100k people without even getting close to risking a food crunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T12:13:58-07:00","id":1460565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460562#post1460562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those numbers support anything close to needing a 1:100k ratio inside a city.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the basics... one vampire feeding on 2 BP/night at the same rate as the Red Cross indicates is safe to donate a &quot;Double Red&quot; (2 pints); once every 16 weeks; is <b>112</b> individuals. This is basically a 1 BP/night plus periodic excess use to the tune of 365 extra blood points per year.<br /> <br /> Now let's see what it would take to get there.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the basics... let's limit ourselves to just the population between According to the <a href=\"https://www.census.gov/data/tables/2019/demo/age-and-sex/2019-age-sex-composition.html\" target=\"_blank\">US Census</a> in the United States the population between the ages of 21-44 is 31.9%. So, out of 100k individuals the vampiric preference in #6 above is a population of <b>31,900</b> individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, lets throw out the percentage who are married, since they're far less likely to be in the establishments a vampire would be hunting at at the hours a vampire is looking for a meal. Again per the census that ranges from 31.5% married in the 25-29 age group, to 66% in the 40-45 age group. Let's use the 66% just because it will cut down the population the most... so of the 31,900 people you've got at least <b>10,846</b> people who are single and between the ages of 21-44.<br /> <br /> Let's further take another 90% off that just for all the other potential factors; too sick, too ugly, incompatible work schedule, shut-ins, etc. This is an extreme, just as using the highest marriage rate above to exclude potential targets was... but its to prove the point. Having access to just 10% of the single 21-44 year olds in a population of 100k still leaves you with <b>1085</b> people... and a single vampire needs only 112 to obtain 2 BP/day without endangering those they're feeding from. If you did a new target every night it would take you nearly three years to get through that 10%.<br /> <br /> And that's being extremely conservative. A more likely number is probably 3-5000+ available happy meals on legs per 100k of the human population and more than enough to support 10-12 vampires per 100k people without even getting close to risking a food crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which leaves the most important number of them all: that you can feed on all these without tipping off any humans that you're doing it that reveals the existence of vampires and results in a massive Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Because not only do you need all of the blood here above but you need to do it in such a way that the existence of vampires is never even expected.<br /> <br /> Maybe not 1:100K but closer.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T13:45:22-07:00","id":1460576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460565#post1460565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which leaves the most important number of them all: that you can feed on all these without tipping off any humans that you're doing it that reveals the existence of vampires and results in a massive Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Because not only do you need all of the blood here above but you need to do it in such a way that the existence of vampires is never even expected.<br /> <br /> Maybe not 1:100K but closer.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you been to a nightclub/rave or had any contact with hookup culture in the last two decades? Given the nature of The Kiss, feeding is no more difficult or notable than scoring a quickie in a dark corner and depending on how freely the alcohol and drugs are flowing that doesn\u2019t take much more than a pulse.<br /> <br /> One of my players openly mocks the ease of feeding by using Tinder (the dating/hookup ap) as the vampire equivalent of GrubHub (\u201cdo I want Mexican or Chinese tonight?\u201d). Bite down during hookup sex and the target has an orgasmic experience and leaves a bit light-headed, none the wiser and probably more than willing to swing by again if you called them up.<br /> <br /> Honestly, an easier way to calculate a vampire population than some ratio is just count the number of night clubs and bars in the city and double that to account for alternate feeding methods and venues large enough to support multiple vampires.<br /> <br /> The only way 1:100k makes sense is if vampires are regularly killing their victims a dozen or more times a year (the current annual death rate in the US is 897 per 100,000... so an extra dozen would be well within the range of sampling errors), but unless you\u2019re playing V5 where the only way to fully satiate your hunger is murder that\u2019s just one of \u201closer\u201d methods of hunting (because it leaves evidence behind) vs. slurping down a couple pints every other night or so with no one the wiser.<br /> <br /> Which is the real irony for me since V5 heavily pushes for lower ratios like the 1:10k or 1:3k I mentioned in its core book when the need to actually murder to fully satiate makes 1:100k more sensible... while V1-V20 uses 1:100k even though vampires could be fully satiated without ever leaving a body in those editions.<br /> <br /> And just to be clear, my population numbers and their plausibility are based off V20 rules since I don\u2019t play V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T15:49:29-07:00","id":1460586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460553#post1460553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* one thing that made the population issue readily apparent was when my group moved to Discord due to Covid and someone started putting together a Google Earth project marking key territories and sites for the city... and we started seeing all the local bars and nightclubs and other prime hunting grounds dotting the city. It really makes the 1:100k number feel like it was pulled out of the ether by a bunch of people who\u2019d never lived in a big city (even a sleepy midwestern one like mine) and explored it\u2019s nightlife and got all their ideas from reading about city life in the 90\u2019s from books printed in the 80\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>An... no. If you search the old threads on this forum you'll find the ones where this matter was discussed extensively, and although their numbers are indeed quite conservative, they're certainly not from the ether.<br /> <br /> Just to begin with, I want to make t clear that your ratio isn't necessarily a problem. If it works for your chronicle and doesn't breaks verisimilitude for your troupe, that's perfectly fine. And I do think that 5k to 10k can work as a high pressure environment, that seems to be your goal.<br /> <br /> But just counting up the number of nightclubs ignores too many factors, because as you feed from club-goers you reduce the number of available club-goers.<br /> <br /> Other resources aside, you need enough people to feed regularly, without accidents causing population pressure, limiting yourself to relatively easy prey, not causing constant health conditions, and do this consistently and indefinitely. 112 valid targets isn't a reasonable minimum, it is the bare minimum to not kill your prey through draining alone while you sip 1 BP every night. But you're not the only thing affecting their health and survival prospect, your feeding isn't even and deeper feeding in a single vessel increases the recovery time exponentially, not linearly, and they must do other things in their lives than just be your vessels.<br /> <br /> Given that this is off-topic and it's working for you, I only recommend that you search for previous discussions in the topic from some years ago. I personally use 50k as a basis, with variations based on several aspects, but another thing is to think about those numbers distribution. If a city is a hub, for example, it can sustain more vampires on the people that travels through. If a given rural area have several towns within one hour of travel of each other, then it can count as a single city for this calculation. And the towns within up to 3 hours of travel may form a somewhat unified vampire society under a single Prince.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460554#post1460554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of points:<br /> <br /> 1. In the World of Darkness, it is very likely the term &quot;Anarch&quot; among vampires isn't a reference to anarchism as a political philosophy. The Anarchist political philosophy was a product of the 18th century but vampire Anarchs referred to as Anarchs have existed since the 12th century (600 years earlier). Vampire Anarchs is thus likely to be a reference to &quot;The Anarchy&quot; of England in all likelihood (1135 to 1153) during the Civil War of King Stephen and Empress Matilda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/BattleOf_Lincoln.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\"> The Anarchy - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Anarchy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The term &quot;Anarch&quot; is thus a pejorative of vampires referring to the fact that individual vampires were revolting against the natural order of their Elders and a breakdown of formal vampire society. It is something that said revoltees would take as a badge of honor symbolizing their defiance against the Law of Caine.<br /> <br /> 2. Anarchs don't have to be a traditional nation state to win against the Camarilla. They also don't have to have much in the way of organization or even shared ideals to work together. The relatively small numbers of vampires and their secrecy means that really they just need to share a limited amount of resources across global lines (which is a lot easier in the Modern Era) to work against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As we've seen with Marcus Vitel, Emperor of Washington D.C., you might even have an incredibly despotic Lasombra Methuselah as a &quot;Anarch&quot; as long as he's paying for the revolution elsewhere. Certainly, the Soviet Union sponsored a lot of revolutions elsewhere and Anarchs Unbound retconned the Brujah Council to be financing Anarchs far and abroad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some notes:<br /> <br /> 1- OoC I'm pretty sure the authors meant the Anarchist political philosophy when they created the Anarchs. That isn't a fact in the setting, but helps to contextualize it.<br /> <br /> 2- Most vampires aren't elders, so in-character the term isn't necessarily applied today in the same sense that it was in the 12th century.<br /> <br /> 3- Lack of cohesion means that they also lack a unified definition of what &quot;winning&quot; is.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that the Anarchs can win against the Camarilla, but without a cohesive center it just means that they can force their own agendas here and there, but seldom will they actually destroy or expel the Camarilla from a given city. First because many don't want that, they just want to change the Prince, or force a change in a given local policy, or any number of other things. Those aren't, by the way, cheap or hollow victories just because the Cam is still there, actually a city where the Prince have to actually listen to the Anarchs and consider their opinions is a pretty neat victory. Second because they have no power structure to replace it, so the Cam is what they have anyway.<br /> <br /> But if they actually expel the Camarilla, then it shifts from fighting the Cam to administrating territory, making and applying laws and dealing with criminals, invaders and such. Then it becomes far more complex than actually fighting the Cam. And then powerful individuals may be ready for the task, but the Anarchs as a system aren't and probably won't be so unified to offer continuous help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T15:54:18-07:00","id":1460587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460586#post1460586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- OoC I'm pretty sure the authors meant the Anarchist political philosophy when they created the Anarchs. That isn't a fact in the setting, but helps to contextualize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but the Anarchs are referred to as such in universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2- Most vampires aren't elders, so in-character the term isn't necessarily applied today in the same sense that it was in the 12th century. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but the thing is that Anarchs from the 12th century are still around too and influencing politics.<br /> <br /> See: Tyler.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that that I always think its a good idea not to get too into &quot;realism&quot; and just accept the fantastical origins of things of themselves. Which is that Anarch philosophy is a thing that has existed in-universe for 800 years among vampires.<br /> <br /> YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3- Lack of cohesion means that they also lack a unified definition of what &quot;winning&quot; is.<br /> <br /> I totally agree that the Anarchs can win against the Camarilla, but without a cohesive center it just means that they can force their own agendas here and there, but seldom will they actually destroy or expel the Camarilla from a given city. First because many don't want that, they just want to change the Prince, or force a change in a given local policy, or any number of other things. Those aren't, by the way, cheap or hollow victories just because the Cam is still there, actually a city where the Prince have to actually listen to the Anarchs and consider their opinions is a pretty neat victory. Second because they have no power structure to replace it, so the Cam is what they have anyway.<br /> <br /> But if they actually expel the Camarilla, then it shifts from fighting the Cam to administrating territory, making and applying laws and dealing with criminals, invaders and such. Then it becomes far more complex than actually fighting the Cam. And then powerful individuals may be ready for the task, but the Anarchs as a system aren't and probably won't be so unified to offer continuous help. </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's a case of how cynical you wish to be about the subject. If the goal is to provide an idealistic counterpart to the Camarilla then the Anarchs lack of cohesion is absolutely a terrible thing. However, if the goal is to create a balkanized series of independent nations where one Anarch Baron can rise to the top over a region and rule as they wish then that is another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> I've always been fond of the idea that the Camarilla vs. Anarchs is less tyrants vs. freedom fighters and more rival gangs duking it out.<br /> <br /> The Corleones vs. Brazzis.<br /> <br /> There's the rare &quot;better&quot; Anarch but the Godfather with Fangs is a preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T16:11:40-07:00","id":1460590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460587#post1460587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's a case of how cynical you wish to be about the subject. If the goal is to provide an idealistic counterpart to the Camarilla then the Anarchs lack of cohesion is absolutely a terrible thing. However, if the goal is to create a balkanized series of independent nations where one Anarch Baron can rise to the top over a region and rule as they wish then that is another matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thing: using this analogy, the Anarchs aren't a single gang, that's the difference. Marcus Vitel as an Anarch Prince isn't a victory of the gang The Anarchs, it is just a victory of Marcus Vitel and his personal gang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T16:38:06-07:00","id":1460592,"title":"","content":"Yeah, modern Anarchs have all the ups and downs of a decentralized political movement.<br /> <br /> The upside is that there is no head of the snake (it would be difficult but one can hypothetically assassinate the Inner Circle or College of Cardinals) to be cut, it\u2019s difficult to identify threats from non-threats and reconnoiter appropriately, it\u2019s difficult to mobilize again a guerilla force, and no matter what you do the Anarchs you don\u2019t hit can fade away to come back at a better time and odds are a bloody reprisal can be used to radicalize new Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Any serious anarch who doesn\u2019t study Mao is a fool.<br /> <br /> Of course the downsides are that there is a little cohesion outside of Balkanized subcultures within the loosely associated groups that make up the Anarch Movement, they are easier to defeat in detail or to trigger infighting within (leftist organizations in particular are infamous for this), and there are few large scale gains that won\u2019t have to not only enter conflict with the traditional sects and rival Anarchs (see: the Soviet Council and the Anarch Free State).<br /> <br /> However just because the current Anarch Movement trends towards horizontal organization doesn\u2019t make that a fact of life. A charismatic leader could rally a broad coalition of anarch supporters under the right conditions, such as presumably occurred with Jeremy MacNeil and the revolutionary leaders of the Soviet Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T16:45:23-07:00","id":1460594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460590#post1460590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the thing: using this analogy, the Anarchs aren't a single gang, that's the difference. Marcus Vitel as an Anarch Prince isn't a victory of the gang The Anarchs, it is just a victory of Marcus Vitel and his personal gang.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also still benefits the Movement if the goal is to carve up the Camarilla's territories like a cake. The Anarchs benefit because the Camarilla weakens even if the freedom of Washington DC doesn't go up.<br /> <br /> Which is an immensely cynical read of the Movement but not necessarily an incorrect one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T17:56:35-07:00","id":1460600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460587#post1460587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps but the thing is that Anarchs from the 12th century are still around too and influencing politics.<br /> <br /> See: Tyler.<br /> <br /> Which is to say that that I always think its a good idea not to get too into &quot;realism&quot; and just accept the fantastical origins of things of themselves. Which is that Anarch philosophy is a thing that has existed in-universe for 800 years among vampires.<br /> <br /> YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that there wasn't much in the way of Anarch philosophy at first. I read this neat fan description somewhere about what Anarch Lore 5 entailed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know all the shit that went down centuries ago, and why the First Revolt erupted. A brutal combination of the Inquisition, perpetual war between the clans, and a system that allowed for nothing but eternal slavery drove those young vampires to destroy their elders and seize power for themselves. Back then, there was no philosophy, only revenge. It only coalesced into a movement for freedom later, with the rise of democracy and all the philosophies of individualism that have marked Western society since. You can see past the romantic veneer on the First Revolt and see it for what it truly is. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T12:22:56-07:00","id":1460713,"title":"","content":"The Anarch philosophy is simple. Young vampires shouldn't be controlled/enslaved by older vampires. <br /> <br /> Anything more than that, and Anarchs are going to disagree with each other. Of course you do need more than that to organize any kind of society, so Anarchs are going to quarrel over what kind of new society should replace the current one. And many vampires who initially are anarchs when they are wrong are going to think differently once they've become older and more powerful.<br /> <br /> Human political movements and philosophy have very little application to that struggle. The vast differential in powers between elder and younger vampires aren't present in human society. And that fact that everyone dies and opens up positions of leadership for the next generation has no counterpart among immortal vampires. Though of course certain ideas can always translate.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the original Greek word &quot;anarchos&quot; simply means &quot;without an archon&quot;. Archons (meaning &quot;ruler&quot;) were the (sometimes elected) magistrates of Athens and other Greek city states. It simply means without rulers. One of its uses was to describe those years when no magistrate was elected to rule Athens. I wonder if the original writers knew that and selected the term archon as a helper to the Justicars for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T22:39:24-07:00","id":1461156,"title":"","content":"I run a V20 Chronicle set in contemporary times, which takes sporadic direction from V5. No Beckoning, but the Brujah and Gangrel have left the Camarilla. The Anarch Free State controls the cities of Southern California, and a few other American cities like Las Vegas and Indianapolis have become new Free States in the last couple of years. Nevertheless, the Camarilla is more concerned about the Sabbat, with the Sect War raging along the East Coast. The opinion of the Justicars and most Camarilla Elders is that the Anarchs can wait to be dealt with; the loss of a few minor domains out West is no immediate concern to the powerful Elders of Chicago and NYC. For the Camarilla in the West however, the Anarchs are no longer a nuisance to be laughed off. What they lack in organization they make up for in numbers, and recent victories have given them a renewed sense of confidence. <br /> <br /> Fortunately(?), the Anarchs spend as much--really more--time jockying and feuding with each other as they do focusing on the Ivory Tower. Portland, OR, a relatively small city (pop 650k, metro pop 2.6 million, the setting of my chronicle) is home to over 30 Anarchs, divided into at least four gangs. The largest of these gangs has become a miniature Camarilla in its own right, with a Baron who has established a court and holds the licks in her Domain to a stringent set of behavior. Other gangs occupy the ragged edges of the region They hold to a bewildering variety of philosophies and beliefs--various kinds of blood cults, worshipping an Antediluvian/Lilith, filtered through new age or pagan spirituality. While all the Anarchs have nominally promised to aid each other in the face of any aggression from the Camarilla, the smaller gangs would love nothing more than to knock the largest from their pedestal. Not all these Unbound are true believers in The Movement, many are simply Unbound with beliefs or philosophies at odds with rules of the Camarilla (which in my setting, still officially denies the truth of Noddism or existence of so-called Antediluvians). <br /> <br /> tl;dr - My Anarchs are a grab-bag of all kinds of Kindred. They're numerous, powerful and have the Camarilla on the backfoot at least on the West Coast, but there's little to no real unity among them. Attempting any sort of organization across the board would be like herding cats, and requires dealing with types ranging from esoteric blood cults to rambunctious bloodbangers no better than shovelheads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T03:54:15-07:00","id":1461180,"title":"","content":"Previous ed anarchs were disenfranchised rebels against an unjust system pretty interesting dynamic at a local level<br /> <br /> V5 anarchs......[bites lip]<br /> <br /> <br /> V5 Anarchs are founded on the idea of a soft reset back to 1st ed Anarchs vs the 'the man' as the primary conflict of the setting this is either a corporate decision from a company who release buggy overpriced dlc and game breaking patches on a regular basis or the pet obessions of the designers who seemed dismissive how the setting and game developed over 20 odd years. This hit critical mass with Anarch book which is effectively 20 pages stretched to 200 and a irl representation of why exactly the Sabbat and Carmarilla quickly stole the spotlight. this is a real problem as for the supposed protagonists the Anarchs are crimminally undeverloped vs the antagonists. With this in mind I've done a large scale re-write of the Anarchs to make them a viable threat to the Carmarilla and the Sabbat. Here are the big changes I implimented.<br /> <br /> 1) The Anarchs form of governance is direct democracy on a local level with the Assembly forming a parliment of sorts, this allows a meaningful distinction in how the sect operates vs the Carmarilla, the Baron is closer to a magistrate/style style figure whose obligation is to engage in day to day sect bullshit but is accountable to the peoples Assembly. The relatively smaller numbers of kindred make this far more viable and yes I am aware it will be a shitshow. their is a talk of representative democracy as a pan-city level but this is in early development<br /> <br /> 2)anarchs have a mixture of Civil liberties and obligations<br /> <br /> Liberties<br /> -Total freedom of speech outside of the advocation of treason or murder of sect mates<br /> -Right to disciplines, no clan may hold monopolies on disciplines... learning them is another issue<br /> -freedom of bloodline/freedom from bloodline, all clans are welcome in the sect and no vampire is expected to show clan loyalty if they do not wish to.<br /> -Right to life no sectmate may murder another, execution must be sanctioned by the Baron and/or the Assembly<br /> -Partial freedom of embrace, Vampires may embrace who they wish however bad embraces is a crime andwill result in censorship or death if found guilty by the Assembly<br /> -Freedom of religion, Vampire may follow paths and alternative religious perspective unless explicitly prohibited by the local assembly.<br /> <br /> Obligations<br /> -All Vampires must defend the free states in times of war.<br /> -Freedom from dominion-No Vampire may control more than 10% of a cities territory as domain, no more than 50% of a city may be privatly held by kindred. Property rights are however respected and haven is sacrosanct<br /> -All other sects are enemies of the Anarch revolution any vampire engaging or aiding other sects is a traitor to the people. the Hecata are considered a neutral 3rd party and are formally invited to join the Anarch cause but no aid may be provided them at the expense of sectmates.<br /> -All Anarchs must serve at least once a year in the Assembly, additional services are expected.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3)Anarchs have a Pagan vibe in contrast to the Catholic Sabbat and the Secular Carmarilla (I'm scraping the faith stuff in V5 its stupid and does nothing), while not a legal issue their is a strong cultural bias from the three major clans as well as dissident bloodlines, the only exceptions is a strong contingent of Lilith defectors from the Sabbat who obviously follow a weird abrahamic heresy and a strong gnostic minority/<br /> <br /> 4)Anarchs as a sect don't really mesh with human politics, they might have some overlaps of interest but no irl group can really present their concerns-for example while Anarchs are anti police it's mostly so they can get away with killing, stealing from and exploiting humans unapposed by armed proffesionals. General sect policy towards humans is 'animal wellfare' were utilization/exploitation is norm but brutalization and cruelty is discouraged<br /> <br /> 5)Brujah, Setite and Gangrel Eldars/anchille are a prominant group in the sect with them being responsable for a lot of the strutural organization, The dynamic is generally less toxic than Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 6)Anarch success is currently due to the descimation of the Sabbat and Carmarilla in the 2nd inquisition. Effectively the sect has often found itself winning by default. As the 2 inquisitions is slowly dying down. The sect is very likely to come under increasing pressure from attempts to re-take lost cities by both sect.<br /> <br /> 7)Masquarade is taken very seriously, a lot of mid 10's sect set backs were due to inquisition purges. Now the sect has a specific coverup culture and titles for that duty.<br /> <br /> Hope people find this useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-24-2021, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T04:58:05-07:00","id":1461185,"title":"","content":"Ugh, Another Pagan Anarch fan. I get it, I do, but no. The Sabbat are Catholic, The Camarilla are Secular (secret cults nonwithstanding), and the Anarchs are religious freedom. Anarchs may have Noddists,Bahari, Antideluvian/methuselah worshippers, Gehenna cultists, new age cults, old religion faiths, infernalism, the religious idea that the kindred condition is purely answerable by science... and so on and so forth. You can even have schisms between these fellows; two bahari cults may see eachother as dangerous and vile heretics spreading false dogma.<br /> <br /> In a city with no Camarilla, there may be any of the following.<br /> <br /> Cults<br /> Gangs/Coteries/Packs<br /> Families.<br /> Fuedal lords<br /> Tiny sects that want to expand.<br /> Counter Revolutionaries (including both actual-camarilla agents and folks who just like the idea of law and order and imagine themselves propped up by the new regime)<br /> Independent clans.<br /> Cartels, companies or protection leagues.<br /> Any kind of overseeing governing body<br /> People who believe might-makes right.<br /> <br /> An Anarch Domain gives you complete freedom to do what you want (at least till the Camarilla come knocking)<br /> The mess makes them a little unustainable though and most of these things can be achieved with the more sustainable and need-less-explaining Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-24-2021, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T05:43:06-07:00","id":1461190,"title":"","content":"Its more of a cultural rather than institutional vibe and fairly easy to remove if I wanted. I'd also like to comment the paganism would be actual historic paganism, not 90's counter culture &quot;like mother nature and weed&quot; pop culture paganism or the circle of crone gritty reboot (weakest written of the 5 from requiem). For example the brujah would have a strong neo platonic Streek. <br /> A good alternative is to make them secular if you're going for the religious v5 carmarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T09:22:34-07:00","id":1461230,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, setting my game in Oregon I felt like if there was anywhere you WOULD have whole gangs of Anarchs into the new age momma-earth-and-weed style of paganism, it'd be here. One of the Anarch crews in Portland, called the Greenfangs, believes that the Kindreds' Frenzy is exacerbated by the unhealthiness of their modern human vessels. Hence they only feed from vegetarians, or better yet vegans, or at least people who eat only organic and fresh produce (large amounts of THC in the vessel's body is also believed to quiet the Beast and the Greenfangs make sure their herd never lacks for the substance). Behind this, the Greenfangs have a confused mix of mythology, having some distorted, thirdhand Bahari myths which they've conflated with Ennoia &quot;the female half of god,&quot; whom they believe to literally be one with the earth and thus what some call Gaia. This isn't getting into the ones who are secret disciples of the Diamond Thunderbolt (a blood-orgy cult based on degenerated tantric rites) or the guy who thinks all Kindred should leave the cities and create a homeostatic utopia of one vampire per collective farm,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T03:29:06-07:00","id":1461659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460553#post1460553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really makes the 1:100k number feel like it was pulled out of the ether by a bunch of people who\u2019d never lived in a big city (even a sleepy midwestern one like mine) and explored it\u2019s nightlife and got all their ideas from reading about city life in the 90\u2019s from books printed in the 80\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is an extremely difficult position to argue for, given what is actually written in the early books. From the 2nd Edition core, page 30 (emphasis mine):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Kindred take no part in the society of the Damned, and maintain no connection with others of their kind. They are known as the Clanless, or the Caitiff. <b>Cities are extremely large places and it is not difficult to isolate oneself from one's peers; indeed, it is said that the only Kindred who ever meet are the ones who wish to meet.</b> However, sometimes even the most solitary vampires can be thrust into the politics of the day -- in times of need, the Caitiff are mercilessly rooted out and questioned. </div> </div> </div><i>The only Kindred who ever meet are the ones who wish to meet.</i> This is one of the basic assumptions of the early edition setting. The impression I get of the original writers is that, rather than pulling numbers and ideas out of the ether with no real life experience with big cities, they took the concept of the Masquerade seriously. More seriously, I would argue, than the idea is treated in the later game line. The famous Kindred to mortal ratio of 1:100,000 -- which was always intended to apply to greater metropolitan areas, not city populations -- is one of the consequences of thinking through the implications of just how plausible the Masquerade would be if vampires really existed in our world.<br /> <br /> I <i>know</i> that it is tempting to lower the ratio significantly to make room for all the political factions, cabals, secret societies, cliques, and conspiracies that the setting has since become inundated with. But this is exactly the kind of impulse that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a> called out in another recent thread: <i>&quot;Writing about the game world has slipped from concrete work on specific places, characters, and experiences, to generalised writing about clans.&quot;</i> Personally, I have a great dislike for this sort of approach, and I would seriously urge anyone populating a metropolitan area for their chronicle to consider how rare vampires really were supposed to be in the beginning. Think about specific characters, not Random Ventrue #7 that you need in order to fill out, say, the ridiculously bloated number of official positions within the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> If it is true that the anarchs don't make sense as a faction in a world where the 1:100,000 ratio of Kindred to mortals is true, my preference would be to modify the idea of the anarchs instead of overpopulating the setting with faceless NPCs just to swell up the ranks of each faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T06:47:51-07:00","id":1461673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461659#post1461659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it is true that the anarchs don't make sense as a faction in a world where the 1:100,000 ratio of Kindred to mortals is true, my preference would be to modify the idea of the anarchs instead of overpopulating the setting with faceless NPCs just to swell up the ranks of each faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends if you think the motive of Anarchs is territory versus being persecuted for other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:54:45-07:00","id":1461684,"title":"","content":"Really, you could have all sorts of arrangements in an individual city and still count as being loyal to the Camarilla. If you have a small group of vampires who set up shop in a town with no vampires and decide to share the resources equally there (as far fetched as that would be) then they can. If a Camarilla Archon shows up, they identify the leader or eldest among them as the prince, show say (honestly) that they aren't breaking the Masquerade or associating with the Sabbat or other enemies of the Camarilla, then the Archon really isn't in any position to report them or complain. The Archon isn't going to say &quot;Hey prince, you aren't oppressing the neonates enough.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:59:56-07:00","id":1461686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461684#post1461684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, you could have all sorts of arrangements in an individual city and still count as being loyal to the Camarilla. If you have a small group of vampires who set up shop in a town with no vampires and decide to share the resources equally there (as far fetched as that would be) then they can. If a Camarilla Archon shows up, they identify the leader or eldest among them as the prince, show say (honestly) that they aren't breaking the Masquerade or associating with the Sabbat or other enemies of the Camarilla, then the Archon really isn't in any position to report them or complain. The Archon isn't going to say &quot;Hey prince, you aren't oppressing the neonates enough.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In a &quot;The Camarilla are reasonable&quot; setting, no. Though that's literally the premise for Berlin in V5. The Camarilla felt like Prince William Waldburg was not showing sufficient zeal in persecuting the Anarchs and replaced him.<br /> <br /> So immediately the Anarchs revolted and overthrew the Camarilla in the city.<br /> <br /> Which either makes the Camarilla look like idiots or reflects a larger plan. It's also possible they were overcompensating for perceived weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T08:51:29-07:00","id":1461694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461673#post1461673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends if you think the motive of Anarchs is territory versus being persecuted for other reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. For clarity's sake, I don't actually agree with the idea that the anarchs presented in the early books don't make sense in a setting sparsely populated with vampires. I was merely entertaining the idea for the sake of the argument. Even the paragraph from the 2nd Edition core book that I quoted above goes on to say that Justicars have been known to make scapegoats out of solitary vampires they find, pinning the crimes of others on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T10:19:09-07:00","id":1461710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461659#post1461659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>know</i> that it is tempting to lower the ratio significantly to make room for all the political factions, cabals, secret societies, cliques, and conspiracies that the setting has since become inundated with. But this is exactly the kind of impulse that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a> called out in another recent thread: <i>&quot;Writing about the game world has slipped from concrete work on specific places, characters, and experiences, to generalised writing about clans.&quot;</i> Personally, I have a great dislike for this sort of approach, and I would seriously urge anyone populating a metropolitan area for their chronicle to consider how rare vampires really were supposed to be in the beginning. Think about specific characters, not Random Ventrue #7 that you need in order to fill out, say, the ridiculously bloated number of official positions within the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the issue I have is that, once you count the 5-6 PCs, there's almost no place that can have sufficient numbers for any meaningful politics. When your PCs account for an eighth of the ideal vampire population is a metro area as big as Boston's (4.8 million or 48 ideal vampires) there's just not enough to work with unless you go busting ratios. One coiterie and on coiterie battle to the death would take out 10-15% of the city's whole vampire population; one heavy action adventure could wipe out half the vampires in a city in a night.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that my preferred GM style is a sandbox (i.e. set up a world with events going on and let the PCs find their own adventures within it via their own choices) so I design based on what the city needs for interesting stories to happen and having more than I need because the PCs won't find them all. Potential enemies need mooks. PCs need potential allies. My campaign started with more detailed NPCs than the chosen metropolitan area (4.8 million) could hold at the 1:100k ratio. By detailed I mean names, generations, natures/demeanors, virtues, humanity/path, willpower, disciplines, their resources and their desires.<br /> <br /> There was no room for meaningful Anarchs without lowering the ratio and the leaders of the Camarilla have no one to even boss around unless you lower it still further after that (what's the point of leaders without underlings) and every vampire on vampire fight to the death was going to be against a named and detailed NPC if I kept to 100k. Boston is also one of the oldest cities in the US (est. 1630) too so the idea that its not at least partially operating on pre-Industrial Revolution assumptions (the IR wouldn't kick off for another century and the Convention of Thorns hadn't even been dry for two centuries when the vampires started making Boston their home).<br /> <br /> 1:100k is great if you're running a short duration campaign or one where most of the characters stand around talking like its a LARP. Once you throw any degree of recurring vampire on vampire violence into it you've got barely enough vampire antagonists for a two-hour action flick even in larger metro areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:00:29-07:00","id":1461718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461659#post1461659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is true that the anarchs don't make sense as a faction in a world where the 1:100,000 ratio of Kindred to mortals is true, my preference would be to modify the idea of the anarchs instead of overpopulating the setting with faceless NPCs just to swell up the ranks of each faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Anarchs don't make sense in this world, but a &quot;realistic version&quot; of any city just can't be a place where you expect everything in the supplements to exist simultaneously. The full Camarilla hierarchy, as an example, isn't supposed to <i>exist</i> in most cities, just on the really big ones. Most cities have the Prince and maybe a Sheriff. Kindred society is supposed to feel constrained, claustrophobic, you're dealing with the same people all the time. Thinking about the game Bloodlines it doesn't represent you meeting several key Kindred of the city, you're supposed to meet literally everyone, and even then is a frigging bloated city due to many tings happening as of late.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461710#post1461710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you throw any degree of recurring vampire on vampire violence into it you've got barely enough vampire antagonists for a two-hour action flick even in larger metro areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You play every instance of violence as a fight to the death? Are your NPCs that suicidal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:13:50-07:00","id":1461721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461710#post1461710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the issue I have is that, once you count the 5-6 PCs, there's almost no place that can have sufficient numbers for any meaningful politics. When your PCs account for an eighth of the ideal vampire population is a metro area as big as Boston's (4.8 million or 48 ideal vampires) there's just not enough to work with unless you go busting ratios. One coiterie and on coiterie battle to the death would take out 10-15% of the city's whole vampire population; one heavy action adventure could wipe out half the vampires in a city in a night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a fine illustration of the various assumptions that different people bring to the game. I have always approached <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> with the premise that lethal violence against other vampires is, because of the way the Humanity rules work, always a Very Big Deal. Wiping out your opposition should be way down on the list of options for the coterie in just about every given situation. Vampires are simply not common enough to be staked and burned on a nightly basis, and no vampire struggling to maintain their Humanity would engage in such bloodshed. Moreoever, I try to never relegate actual vampires to the status of mooks. A vampire leader's mooks <i>should not be other vampires.</i> That's a role that ghouls should play.<br /> <br /> So, yes -- if I were to do a <i>Boston by Night</i> chronicle, I would start with the assumption that there are around 50 Kindred in the Greater Boston area, plus all their non-Kindred lackeys, and work from there. What would the politics of the place look like? The number of vampires is probably not enough to support the kinds of conflict that you see in the largest population centers of the World of Darkness, but not every city in the US needs to look like <i>Chicago by Night.</i> That book was never supposed to be a template for how the rest of the World of Darkness worked, but an example of a failed, borderline overpopulated city on the brink of collapse.<br /> <br /> My problem with busting open the ratio of vampires to mortals is that when it comes to the larger population centers of the world, the number of vampires is quickly inflated to ludicrous levels. Take one of the classic Sabbat strongholds of the setting, Mexico City. Even using the conservative 1:100,000 ratio, the Mexico City metropolitan area is populous enough to support at least 160 Cainites. How many detailed NPCs with individual writeups did the 2002 <i>Mexico City by Night</i> have? About <i>forty.</i> Even if you took all the NPCs from <i>Mexico City by Night</i> and put them together with the 100 characters from the original <i>Chicago by Night</i>, you would still not get to 160!<br /> <br /> Using the Revised era suggestion of 1 Cainite for every 50,000 mortals in Sabbat-controlled cities makes the numbers grow even more out of control. The mind boggles at the chronicle where you would need to stat up <b><i>320</i></b> individual Sabbat vampires in Mexico City before you even begin play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:15:53-07:00","id":1461722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461718#post1461718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Anarchs don't make sense in this world, but a &quot;realistic version&quot; of any city just can't be a place where you expect everything in the supplements to exist simultaneously. The full Camarilla hierarchy, as an example, isn't supposed to <i>exist</i> in most cities, just on the really big ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Very</i> much agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:28:06-07:00","id":1461727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461722#post1461722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Very</i> much agreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the days of the original White Wolf forums, I described Vampire as a game that was, theoretically meant to function like &quot;Friends.&quot;<br /> <br /> No, seriously. Forget fighting Sabbat and ancient conspiracies. The game's premise would be you and your coterie would go to the Succubus Club and then somehow get roped into the latest plot of one of the NPCs in Chicago or whatever your city was. The number of vampires in the city meant that you would know every single one of them and a newcomer would be fairly rare.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> 1. The Prince wants to burn down a district of poor minorities and as Anarchs it's up to you to thwart him.<br /> <br /> 2. The Tremere Chantry member wants you to rob an old man of a magical artifact. It turns out he's a wizard.<br /> <br /> 3. The Anarch leader has killed a visiting Anarch's ghoul in a frenzy. You need to dispose of it like Goodfellas before you realize they're going to blame you.<br /> <br /> In other words a lot more intimate and small scale setting than most RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:39:21-07:00","id":1461732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461710#post1461710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the issue I have is that, once you count the 5-6 PCs,</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say, though, to meet you in the middle, that I don't count the PC coterie among the vampire population of a given city. The PCs are extra characters added on top of the existing society, so the actual number of vampires in the chronicle is likely to be slightly higher than strict adherence to the 1:100,000 ratio would produce. I don't hold the ratio sacred, I just use it as a guideline for thinking about the structure and politics of a given city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:12:15-07:00","id":1461743,"title":"","content":"It'd be hard to kill off a sizable city. Most vampires are spread out and either hidden, well protected, or both. If you really put effort into finding out where all the malks are, they'll be onto you, and they'll move. Cities are big and it'd be hard to strike at everyone before alarms ring. Elysiums, like... do you want to live? If you could somehow pull off killing all the vampires in elysium, I imagine someone crazy with ideas about the sanctity of Elysium will have you hounded till the end of the earth.<br /> <br /> RE- Population<br /> I actually inflate the mortal population and overall size of cities to support more vampires. Not to say that I use 1:100,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:29:20-07:00","id":1461746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461727#post1461727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the days of the original White Wolf forums, I described Vampire as a game that was, theoretically meant to function like &quot;Friends.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like that.<br /> <br /> The big time politics happen in the long run as you trade info with contacts outside the city, something not everyone in the city do. But in the city proper you have the same characters coming up with new shenanigans again and again and again.<br /> <br /> It is a vicious relationship: those are your enemies, but also your company for the long eternity. They're going to stab you. You're going to stab them. You'll all meet at Elysium after that, for the rest of the century. Rinse and repeat until you tire of those faces and, yet, fear to lose those few constants on your life. Even low Humanity vampires are loath on killing others of their kind. Manipulating, torturing, deceiving, abusing, all of that is fair play. Kill? And face your own mortality and the inexorable course of time towards the unknown? Not so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461743#post1461743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE- Population<br /> I actually inflate the mortal population and overall size of cities to support more vampires. Not to say that I use 1:100,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also that big time. The World of Darkness is supposed to be ours but worse, and it includes more packed and full.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:29:42-07:00","id":1461747,"title":"","content":"A good rule of thumb for me that I use is:<br /> <br /> &quot;Small towns and underpopulated cities often have no Kindred whatsoever while large cities with thriving nightlife have 3x4 times the size of their recommended numbers at the least. However, most vampire cities never rise beyond a population of 100-200 Camarilla/Anarch Kindred. Everyone knows everyone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> In terms of Anarchs there's usually only a gang or two of 6-20 vampires with the latter likely to split in two.<br /> <br /> Most Kindred are NOT Anarchs OR Camarilla but just sort of in the middle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461746#post1461746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like that.<br /> <br /> The big time politics happen in the long run as you trade info with contacts outside the city, something not everyone in the city do. But in the city proper you have the same characters coming up with new shenanigans again and again and again.<br /> <br /> It is a vicious relationship: those are your enemies, but also your company for the long eternity. They're going to stab you. You're going to stab them. You'll all meet at Elysium after that, for the rest of the century. Rinse and repeat until you tire of those faces and, yet, fear to lose those few constants on your life. Even low Humanity vampires are loath on killing others of their kind. Manipulating, torturing, deceiving, abusing, all of that is fair play. Kill? And face your own mortality and the inexorable course of time towards the unknown? Not so much.<br /> <br /> Also that big time. The World of Darkness is supposed to be ours but worse, and it includes more packed and full.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the thing about Bloodlines that it did capture well as the idea that the Prince was supposed to be your archenemy and employer at once sometimes. At least if he was based on Lodin and that was how I figured he was supposed to be. The Prince is someone too powerful for you to kill but wasn't going to kill you directly unless you really screwed up.<br /> <br /> There was a dance going on of defiance and submission until one of you gained the upper hand.<br /> <br /> A lot of my early campaigns reached the climax of, &quot;Okay, you've finally got a Blood Hunt on you. You can either stay and try to kill the Prince to seize power and hope the next one is more inclined to like you post-regicide or flee to another city.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-27-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:05:00-07:00","id":1461752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461718#post1461718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You play every instance of violence as a fight to the death? Are your NPCs that suicidal?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the PCs and the system tend to be just that lethal. Just about every campaign I've run has included at least one PC who can virtually (or completely on a good roll) one-shot anything that can't soak significant amounts of aggravated damage. The only thing that has prevented mass death in my present campaign is that the one with the monopoly on the use of force in the party is genuinely humane (rather than self-righteously so).<br /> <br /> In another case, one of my players was ex-military and served in Iraq. He didn't plan around anything less than complete and utter annihilation of a potential opponent. If they had time to fight back or warn others; you were doing it wrong in his book. &quot;Fair fights are for losers,&quot; was his motto. Yes, his PC's Humanity was 2 (no degeneration checks needed for pre-meditated murder). He didn't care. His PC would have gone onto (or more realistically started on) the Path of Honorable Accord in a heartbeat if I'd let him because he felt it better reflected his real life values.<br /> <br /> This dips a bit into the &quot;how bad are your vampires&quot; territory, but if the PCs decide violence is the answer to the problem the system isn't built for there to be survivors in the fights unless the victors (PC or NPC) want there to be survivors. So, as a rule, I keep enough &quot;extras&quot; around just in case the players dive into that end of the sandbox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:17:18-07:00","id":1461755,"title":"","content":"Use V1/2 rules for aggravated soak. <br /> I don't have an answer for large scale explosives or military-level weapons, other than restricting access to the later and banning chemists. <br /> <br /> I think such a violent character might get whacked for &quot;the safety of the sect&quot;. A Humanity 2 neonate among the cam is a wight in waiting, and not that much better off in most Anarch circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:32:22-07:00","id":1461758,"title":"","content":"Plenty of Anarchs do the whole &quot;fight it out&quot; thing but in my games, it's never lethal. Anarchs aren't the Sabbat and engaged in monomancy. If they have two Brujah going at it with Celerity and Potence then its until one of them can't fight anymore and usually not until Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:37:26-07:00","id":1461760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461752#post1461752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This dips a bit into the &quot;how bad are your vampires&quot; territory, but if the PCs decide violence is the answer to the problem the system isn't built for there to be survivors in the fights unless the victors (PC or NPC) want there to be survivors. So, as a rule, I keep enough &quot;extras&quot; around just in case the players dive into that end of the sandbox.</div> </div> </div> </div>On my games such level of violence would result in an almost instant Blood Hunt. I won't judge your player because I know how much US military training uses the most advanced techniques to break a person into a killing machine and don't bother to even try to rebuild. But as in real life he needs to understand that those aren't the rules of this society and there will be consequences for breaking them. The moment this psycho makes the first victim the Prince should be wary of letting him live to make another.<br /> <br /> But in the end I think Vampire may simply not be the right game for this person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T09:01:56-07:00","id":1461829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461760#post1461760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my games such level of violence would result in an almost instant Blood Hunt\u2026 The moment this psycho makes the first victim the Prince should be wary of letting him live to make another.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Prince was the guy\u2019s biggest fan. Do not confuse \u201cuse of violence\u201d for \u201cindiscriminate slaughter.\u201d<br /> <br /> One of the first things the new PC did (back when they still had Humanity 5) was learn which vampires were causing the Prince problems, picked a particularly charismatic Anarch, tracked him down over the course of several nights and blew his head into red mist with a .50 BMG sniper rifle from 1200 yards.<br /> <br /> He then went to the Prince and used his kill of a target that had been causing problems as the start of his r\u00e9sum\u00e9 for the position of Scourge. He made his rep in the city by removing any problems for the Prince; particularly any would be Anarch leaders, Caitiff, Thinbloods and Sabbat scouting parties.<br /> <br /> Yes, his Humanity was low; he committed pre-meditated murder on a regular basis; but he was not killing at random. He was killing potential threats to the Prince with the sanction of the Prince.<br /> <br /> Humanity 2 is where a professional sniper is going to end up eventually. Every shot is a pre-meditated killing. The military teaches the sniper to justify it as necessary for the greater good, but, as you mentioned, the military is damned effective at stripping away what we\u2019d call Humanity to get effective soldiers who will kill without question or hesitation.*<br /> <br /> And to shift this back more towards the actual topic; since my argument about Anarchs is ultimately about numbers/density I do think it\u2019s relevant to add that while I have a population density of 1:10k in my city setting, my overall global numbers are about 1:100k. <br /> <br /> The ideal hunting grounds for vampires are high density urban areas where pedestrian and mass transit are the default modes of transport for the majority of the population. Having grown up in the Midwest, my view is that there are regions like the American Midwest that are virtually devoid of vampires while others are much higher densities. <br /> <br /> For example, even our large cities in Indiana are highly decentralized (ex. Indianapolis and Fort Wayne in Indiana have a population density of c. 2500/square mile vs. over 14,000 in Boston and 20k+ in places like New York and Miami) with negligible pedestrian or mass transit use.<br /> <br /> The overall population of Indiana is 6.7 million, but there probably aren\u2019t more than a dozen vampires in the state (so 1:500k ratio) because the urban structure doesn\u2019t support as many as places like Boston, New York, Chicago or Miami can.<br /> <br /> The same goes for Illinois (pop 12.6 million) outside Chicago, for most of Ohio (11.7 million), Michigan (10 million) and Wisconsin (5.8 million). Including Indiana that\u2019s 36.8 million people (368 vampires at 1:100k) but the poor hunting due to the decentralized urban landscape means the vampire population may only be 72-ish outside of Chicago in the whole region. Those other 300 vampires are going to instead cluster into the cities with easier hunting conditions resulting in much lower ratios (like my 1:10k) in high density urban areas like Chicago, Boston, New York, Atlantic City, DC, Miami, etc.<br /> <br /> Put another way, by a strict 1:100k ratio there should be over 3300 vampires in the US, but I highly doubt 31 of them are in Iowa (pop 3.1 million) where the largest city\u2019s metro area is just 700k and the next largest is half that.<br /> <br /> Huge swaths of the country and the rural populations therein are basically food deserts for the undead, and if the 1:100k ratio stands those vampires end up on the fringes of your high density urban areas, risking overpopulation by vampire standards and pushing for rights inside the established system.<br /> <br /> There are your Anarchs.<br /> <br /> * It was this player who convinced me that at least some mortal soldiers could more accurately be reflected in game as being on a variation of the Path of Honorable Accord rather than at very low levels of Humanity because it better reflects the alternate system of morality drilled into the modern soldier versus portraying them as merely morally degenerate (with the corresponding inability to present high levels of self-control and courage that low Humanity brings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 09-28-2021, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T10:50:08-07:00","id":1461842,"title":"","content":"This is interesting, but changes nothing. If this scourge is so effective he'll have the job done in short notice. Either his enemies would learn to not be as easy as targets, leave the city, destroy him with as much violence, or be done with quickly. Either way the chronicle would take a turn as he's left without targets or is killed. By just giving him more mooks to kill you're not following the intent of the setting at all. Which is not a problem <i>per se</i> if you have fun, but it's not the setting's fault that the proposed ratio don't serve your purposes.<br /> <br /> Also, any vampire this effective at killing with a vengeance could be loved by the Prince, but what others would expect of him? He's only an asset while tightly under control, otherwise he's a risk. The same goes for the entire group if you feel like the game is too lethal for vampires. The reason a bar fight isn't lethal is because you're not expected to bring shotguns to one. If your players are bringing fire to a fight it's not the system that's too lethal, their characters are psychopaths.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't brush aside rural areas, either. A good chunk of the overall population is on them and most of those people won't travel to large urban centers frequently or at all. You would be effectively discarding a lot of potential prey from the vampiric ecosystem, reducing the effective population for such purposes. And remember that rural/wandering vampires are a thing. Breaking the ratio on rural areas where it still means a small number of vampires in a large geographical area is also a thing.<br /> <br /> Reducing the overall ratio to 1:50k is sensible if you don't want the feel of isolation and loneliness the 1st ed core book went for. And a greater Kindred proportion in travel hubs of all kinds is definitely a thing. But 1:10k is too much as a rule of thumb. Not catastrophic, but already too crowded for anyone's comfort, the kind of place where Embraces and Dominion are tightly controlled and highly disputed, even if it is a travel hub (that may also have to contend with traveling undead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T00:29:56-07:00","id":1461925,"title":"","content":"In most cases, A prince sanctioning a neonate with a sniper rifle on the murder of all the Anarchs will have his home firebombed and his childer murdered. And not necessarily by the surviving Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T07:51:32-07:00","id":1461954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461925#post1461925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases, A prince sanctioning a neonate with a sniper rifle on the murder of all the Anarchs will have his home firebombed and his childer murdered. And not necessarily by the surviving Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the Prince may go, &quot;What a lunatic! I declare a Blood Hunt on this psycho killer!&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I agree. Most vampires would be iffy about a Prince who disposes of all of his opposition so decisively, even if they're not liked. Besides, its a declaration of open warfare.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T08:09:49-07:00","id":1461956,"title":"","content":"A wise prince <i>should </i>go &quot;what a lunatic! I declare a Blood hunt on this psycho killer&quot;, use some other punishment , or at the very least feign ignorance and demand proof that the psycho was doing things on their behalf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back on topic.<br /> The 1:100,000 makes more sense with... dare i talk about it again, the absolute joke of American city planning, with parking lots and auto-centric suburbia as far as the eye can see, and then a crammed downtown that's the only good place to eat. Most of the world's cities are far more efficient with population spread, meaning vampires can decentralize and still have healthy domains, making competition far less fierce and humans can be better used. You could probably sustain 1:5000 if you really wanted to push your prince to madness, in a european city that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-29-2021, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T10:52:16-07:00","id":1461978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461956#post1461956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">parking lots and auto-centric suburbia as far as the eye can see, and then a crammed downtown that's the only good place to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it, you mean &quot;only good place to eat&quot; for vampires or humans? I'm not used to american city planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T11:13:09-07:00","id":1461981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461978#post1461978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it, you mean &quot;only good place to eat&quot; for vampires or humans? I'm not used to american city planning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To put it simply, most American cities are designed for the car, and everything's really far away from everything. This makes it really hard to sculk around because obfuscate has a range limit. Designated drivers protect their drunk mates, and it's hard to find a nice corner. If you go home with someone, or someone goes home with you, a vampire may need to worry about getting back or sending a person away without a taxi driver getting curious about all these drained men coming from the same house. It can be a lot harder to get away with crime (breaking and entering) in suburbs. The parking lots are too big, too open, too exposed to feed in... There's just lots of little inconveniences that add up. On the flipside, American cities often have overdeveloped &quot;downtown&quot; areas with skyscrapers and tall housing filled with the poor. These are great places to feed, which makes overcompetition a real issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T11:19:24-07:00","id":1461982,"title":"","content":"Personally I've never really bothered figuring out population/kindred ratios I just have as many as I need for the plot. or just genrally state if the pop is high or low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-29-2021, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T12:12:31-07:00","id":1461995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461978#post1461978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it, you mean &quot;only good place to eat&quot; for vampires or humans? I'm not used to american city planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might also explain why you didn't quite grok my argument about the American Midwest being a food desert unable to support many vampires despite millions of people.<br /> <br /> Perhaps some pictures will illustrate (and I'll use km instead my more familiar miles since if you're not up on American cities you're probably also not up on our non-metric units of measurement).<br /> <br /> This is Indianapolis, the largest city in Indiana (Metro population 2.1 million; density 947/km^2);<br /> <img src=\"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:40900:40947/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Note all the green in the background; that's single family suburban homes. At the extreme end its farmland.<br /> <br /> This is the second largest city in Indiana, Fort Wayne (metro area 420k, city density 944/km^2);<br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-cc7-HbdPbE/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That green? Again, single family homes fading into farmland. The population density less than 20 miles from the city center drops to under 50/km^2 (as in you'd need a territory about 45 km on a side to support one vampire at 1:100k) outside the city. As an example, Adams County, due south of Fort Wayne is just 41/km^2.<br /> <br /> People from the surrounding communities (i.e. all that territory with 40-50/km^2 people in it) drive up to an hour to an hour and a half to come physically shop here (beyond that they're closer to other large urban areas). Even the general population doesn't actually live in the &quot;dense&quot; urban area... the majority live 16-30 km from where they work and shop. There's no way to get any degree of efficient mass transit to work with a population that geographically spread out... thus, automobiles and parking garages everywhere and almost no pedestrians for easy feeding off of.<br /> <br /> And here's a typical &quot;city&quot; in Indiana; Valparaiso (pop. 33,000; density 740/km^2 in the city limits... same less than 50/km^2 when you hit the green).<br /> <img src=\"https://www.planning-next.com/wp/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Aerial-downtown-Valparaiso-Indiana_700.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> The &quot;nightlife&quot; here is over by 9pm, except on Fridays during Highschool Football season.<br /> <br /> And this is the DENSER population areas of the Midwest. Wisconsin has HALF the population density statewide as Indiana does. Cross the Mississippi River into Iowa and the density is half of Wisconsin's.<br /> <br /> Lots and lots of rural small towns where everyone knows everyone equates to a giant food desert filled with ravening Lupines despite tens of millions of people living there.<br /> <br /> * * * *<br /> <br /> Now, for comparison, here's Boston, MA (Metro Pop 4.8 million; density 5400/km^2)<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/85/12/58/8512585145291044a9152cf660e9d76b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Note particularly the much greater number of multi-story apartments and centralized urban area that brings a much greater concentration of the population together. That's why vampires are much more likely to flock to large high density urban areas rather than the countryside of the Midwest. Its much easier to hide and be anonymous and for people to not realize when someone goes missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T12:30:58-07:00","id":1461998,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the info, I really misinterpreted post #58. It is nice to have the pictures and this is interesting information, but doesn't really changes my mind. You're overly focusing on a few methods of feeding, there are others for suburban and rural areas and they exist everywhere, even if not in the same way. I keep what I said earlier, vampires adapt to every kind of hunting ground and won't discard those spaces just because feeding is different.<br /> <br /> What will happen is that the Kindred feeding on suburbia or wandering the countryside will have other feeding strategies. And certainly the ones in downtown will have an easier way, but easier isn't the same as the only available. Those are likely to be the prime hunting spots vampire fight for, but the vampires losing the fight still need to eat. The bad hunting spots are still a part of vampire ecology and impact that population ratio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T13:50:36-07:00","id":1462004,"title":"","content":"The thing is, that rural vampire could just as easily hit up one of other dozen night clubs in Fort Wayne that the four (at 1:100k vampires) or the homeless shelters or hospitals or perpetual adoration chapels in the one city\u2026 whatever areas the bigger vampires aren\u2019t attending and do so far less riskily than feeding by breaking into a rural home.<br /> <br /> Because here\u2019s the other thing about rural America that non-rural Americans don\u2019t appreciate; we\u2019re ARMED and have security systems in our homes. This is a country with more guns than people and most of those guns don\u2019t reside in the big cities. You may have heard the phrase \u201cwhen seconds count, the police are minutes away\u201d? Try 10-20 minutes in a rural area.<br /> <br /> And at least half the year most people are home before the sun is down or are in their cars driving to church/school events. Everyone knows everyone in the small towns so if someone goes missing, they\u2019re going to notice.<br /> <br /> And have we mentioned the werewolf packs present in the World of Darkness? The ones who prefer the rural areas which are yet another reason why vampires stick to the cities?<br /> <br /> Unless you\u2019re hunting animals for food the rural Midwest is awful and basically a \u201cits this or Final Death\u201d option. Skulking in the shadows of even a small urban area and driving that ratio down is infinitely preferable\u2026 even better a big urban area where adding 1 vampire to the 48 in Boston makes the ratio 1:98k vs. the 1:80k it\u2019d be by adding 1 to the 4 in Fort Wayne.<br /> <br /> Of course, you\u2019re not the only vampire with the same idea so that ratio quickly drops further and the only thing keeping the big cities from being overrun is the Prince putting his foot down on numbers (generally requiring force and a few examples be made) and\u2026 there you have the grounds where Anarchs spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:01:34-07:00","id":1462007,"title":"","content":"Also, just to add and reclarify. I\u2019m not saying there are NO vampires in the rural areas, just that the population density is going to be a lot less than 1:100k. The rest are moving to the shadows of the bigger urban areas looking for easier feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:11:00-07:00","id":1462009,"title":"","content":"I felt I had to share this twice:<br /> <br /> Hypothetical Scenario (Totally not based on one of my games*):<br /> <br /> <b>A Tzimisce joins the Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> Lief, Brujah: So, you're Tzimisce, right?<br /> <br /> Zard, Tzimisce: Shim-A-Shay, yes.<br /> <br /> Lief: So, welcome to the Anarchs. I think you'll find it very different from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Zard: This is my address. *hands business card*<br /> <br /> Lief: What?<br /> <br /> Zard: It is a two-story mansion with an extensive basement that I will be expanded. Do not enter this property upon pain of death. In exchange, I will proceed to offer to alter any and all of your gang's facial features. I can make them blindingly beautiful, different from their mortal identities, or grotesque but I understand most aren't into that.<br /> <br /> Lief: You can't just...what?<br /> <br /> Zard: I will participate in your meetings and also any and all attempts to assassinate Elders or Ancilla of the Camarilla or Sabbat. I will engage in diablerie or not as befitting agreed upon terms ahead of time regarding war spoils. Furthermore, I will not feed on any mortals you personally list but require the feeding on the UCLA Mathematics Department be left to me. Do we have an accord?<br /> <br /> Lief: Uh, sure I guess.<br /> <br /> Zard I find this equitable. Here is a potted plant to symbolize our new status as allies, fellow Anarch.<br /> <br /> Lief: It's bleeding.<br /> <br /> Zard: You're welcome.<br /> <br /> * It's totally based on one of my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:21:19-07:00","id":1462011,"title":"","content":"I imagine that's why a lot of rural vampires are nomad. You'd be hunting at truck stops, roadside diners, highways etc. Liminal spaces where people aren't going to notice if you never come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:25:23-07:00","id":1462014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462011#post1462011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that's why a lot of rural vampires are nomad. You'd be hunting at truck stops, roadside diners, highways etc. Liminal spaces where people aren't going to notice if you never come back.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of my V:TM articles, I said that those went from being ignored domains to highly sought after during Covid-19's shutdowns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T15:26:55-07:00","id":1462024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462004#post1462004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because here\u2019s the other thing about rural America that non-rural Americans don\u2019t appreciate; we\u2019re ARMED and have security systems in our homes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really think the US is the only place in the world where people are armed in the countryside? Just because it is the most extremely legally armed country in the world it doesn't mean it is the only place where country folk have guns.<br /> <br /> My statements stand to the last on my part. What will happen if those vampires try to sneak into the city in droves is precisely that the locals will start to drive them off. And what will happen when some vampires see large rural areas with no undead on them is lack of competition, hence opportunity. Remember that vampires are still humans in some sense, and we colonized deserts. Actual deserts.<br /> <br /> But even then I'm again not saying that the 1:100k ratio must be held sacred or consistent, I'm saying that a 1:10k ratio is too crowded to be a rule of thumb even on a city. Vampires will surely converge to big cities, but not in that big numbers, because there's also a ratio on the mortal population to support those vampires. Indiana may not have 67 vampires (by the 1:100k ratio) because of its small size, but it wouldn't have so much less than that, either, and it wouldn't be because they moved to Boston.<br /> <br /> If any one city have a 1:10k ratio that city is at the tipping point. It is livable, but not good, and a lot of vampires are being driven to feed in the suburbia anyway, even in the surrounding rural areas. Domain distribution won't be fair, and turf will be defended with violence if needed. If it comes to Final Deaths, the Prince is unlikely to issue new Embrace authorizations to the point of getting it do the same crowded ratio again. Because for this Prince the national or global ratio isn't remotely relevant.<br /> <br /> And one final note, I'm not sure if cites outside the US are as different as you think. Sure it isn't the strict suburbia-downtown arrangement, or same amount of parking lots, but you do seems to have some false expectations on the rest of the world. And what get me confused on that post was that at first I thought it was talking about good places for people to eat, not for vampires to eat people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462009#post1462009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt I had to share this twice:<br /> <br /> Hypothetical Scenario (Totally not based on one of my games*):</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I loved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:44:54-07:00","id":1462043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462024#post1462024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indiana may not have 67 vampires (by the 1:100k ratio) because of its small size, but it wouldn't have so much less than that, either, and it wouldn't be because they moved to Boston.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. They\u2019d head for Gary and Chicago, the place that was canonically stated to have had well over a hundred twenty vampires at one point vs. the 60-some it could actually sustain. Funnily enough, that\u2019s about 60 excess vampires or nearly the entire population of Indiana.<br /> <br /> See how that works?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If any one city have a 1:10k ratio that city is at the tipping point. It is livable, but not good, and a lot of vampires are being driven to feed in the suburbia anyway, even in the surrounding rural areas. Domain distribution won't be fair, and turf will be defended with violence if needed. If it comes to Final Deaths, the Prince is unlikely to issue new Embrace authorizations to the point of getting it do the same crowded ratio again. Because for this Prince the national or global ratio isn't remotely relevant. </div> </div> </div>See, I know you think you\u2019re arguing against the 1:10k ratio here, but all I see in this description of a city is \u201ckickass campaign setting! DO IT!!!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T18:13:24-07:00","id":1462051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461686#post1461686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a &amp;quot;The Camarilla are reasonable&amp;quot; setting, no. Though that's literally the premise for Berlin in V5. The Camarilla felt like Prince William Waldburg was not showing sufficient zeal in persecuting the Anarchs and replaced him.<br /> <br /> So immediately the Anarchs revolted and overthrew the Camarilla in the city.<br /> <br /> Which either makes the Camarilla look like idiots or reflects a larger plan. It's also possible they were overcompensating for perceived weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by reasonable. I think that the vampires in charge of the Camarilla are ruthless killers. I also think that they are highly intelligent and crafty elders who have proven themselves over the centuries to be experts in politics, subtlety, manipulation, and human/vampire nature. Vampires who weren\u2019t really good at that stuff wouldn\u2019t have risen to positions of power within the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> I also see the Camarilla as being quite feudal by its nature - notably that the local prince is the authority and as long as he obeys the rules of the Camarilla and maintains order, he will be left alone. Of course, this isn\u2019t universal and perhaps if lenience towards the Anarchs is giving kindred in other cities ideas, or if the city is becoming a haven for those who actively oppose the Camarilla, then the higher ups may have to intervene, but otherwise they should be left alone.<br /> <br /> Of course, even the most Machiavellian elder can make mistakes, but they shouldn\u2019t be in the habit of doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T00:02:05-07:00","id":1462095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462043#post1462043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not. They\u2019d head for Gary and Chicago, the place that was canonically stated to have had well over a hundred twenty vampires at one point vs. the 60-some it could actually sustain. Funnily enough, that\u2019s about 60 excess vampires or nearly the entire population of Indiana.<br /> <br /> See how that works?</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you come up with the number 60? Even back in 1991, when the original core book discussed how the 1:100,000 ratio is supposed to work, the Chicago metropolitan area had around 7 million people, and could thus safely support around 70 vampires. I'll highlight some passages on page 169 that clearly show that the original authors put careful thought into the matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A large city such as San Francisco or Frankfurt normally supports a Vampire population of anywhere from <b>twenty to fifty,</b> depending on circumstances in that city. Larger cities like New York or greater London hold a proportionately larger population and smaller cities much less.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, assume that at the maximum there is one Vampire for every 100,000 mortals. <b>Thus, the greater Chicago metropolitan area, a region of 7 million mortals, can support nearly 70 Vampires.</b> Often a Prince will artificially regulate how many Kindred reside within the city, thus ensuring the sanctity of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <b>The cities could certainly hold more Kindred, but there are legitimate concerns over discovery.</b> The Masquerade is always primary in the minds of the Elders -- better that some Anarchs die than all be extinguished in another Inquisition. Every care is taken to insure that the existence of Vampires is kept secret from the mortal population. Strict controls are kept over the creation of Neonates. Too many Vampires would increase the probability of discovery dramatically. The population is also restricted by the simple fact that <b>few potential Vampires survive their Becoming, many are driven mad by it and put down by their Sire.</b> </div> </div> </div>Since then, the population numbers have only grown, of course, and nowadays the greater Chicago metropolitan area can easily support around a hundred vampires (population of 9.5 million in 2019). I would also remind people that Chicago was always supposed to be overpopulated by vampires. From the back-cover blurb for <i>Chicago by Night:</i> <i>&quot;No other city so dangerously on the edge of chaos. <b>No other city so desperately overcrowded</b>.&quot;</i> Overpopulation is one of the themes of the book, and using Chicago as the yardstick for how every city in the setting is supposed to work actively goes against how the World of Darkness was portrayed in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T03:52:42-07:00","id":1462109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460554#post1460554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of points:<br /> In the World of Darkness, it is very likely the term &quot;Anarch&quot; among vampires isn't a reference to anarchism as a political philosophy. The Anarchist political philosophy was a product of the 18th century but vampire Anarchs referred to as Anarchs have existed since the 12th century (600 years earlier). Vampire Anarchs is thus likely to be a reference to &quot;The Anarchy&quot; of England in all likelihood (1135 to 1153) during the Civil War of King Stephen and Empress Matilda.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder where this idea first saw an appearance in print (hint: you will find the answer in my signature). But this is a problem bequeathed by a careless use of language. The use of the term &quot;Anarch&quot; in the early <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> supplements was clearly a reference to the nineteenth-century political movement, but obviously causes problems if the term is used prior to the nineteenth century.<br /> <br /> Don't get me started on &quot;Justicar&quot;, a spelling mistake which never got corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:03:19-07:00","id":1462112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1460587#post1460587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps but the thing is that Anarchs from the 12th century are still around too and influencing politics.<br /> <br /> See: Tyler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the World of Darkness there are no Anarchs in the twelfth century; their equivalent are Furores and, whilst there is a clear line of descent from the medieval Furore movement to the modern Anarch movement, the two are not identical. Tyler won't even be born until 1352, and will have to wait until 1381 to be embraced. The term &quot;Anarch&quot; will become common currency around the fourteenth and fifteenth centuries, but game resources are not entirely clear about the course of the Anarch Revolt, so it's hard to say exactly when the term becomes established.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T04:41:42-07:00","id":1462117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1461710#post1461710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the issue I have is that, once you count the 5-6 PCs, there's almost no place that can have sufficient numbers for any meaningful politics. When your PCs account for an eighth of the ideal vampire population is a metro area as big as Boston's (4.8 million or 48 ideal vampires) there's just not enough to work with unless you go busting ratios. One coiterie and on coiterie battle to the death would take out 10-15% of the city's whole vampire population; one heavy action adventure could wipe out half the vampires in a city in a night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an idea which I see quite often, broadly defined as a game needs a population of 100 or 200 Cainites to function, particularly in terms of political structures. This is an idea which gets a great deal of implicit support in <i>Vampire </i>supplements from the revised edition onwards. Populations stop being defined, a notion of indefinite number of vampires in a given domain appears, and scales go out the window. Look at the political structures of the Ventrue laid out in the clan's revised clanbook. You have four distinct ranks of Ventrue in any given city; if you assume that there are five vampires at the top rank, each of whom oversee five vampires of the next rank (and that's about the minimum number required at a rank to make sense of the structure) you would end up with 780 Ventrue in the average city. And that's before you end up with the members of any other clan.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, what you end up with when politics is thought of purely in terms of abstract structures and yet, at the same time, there are far more characters for most of them to have any other role than to be &quot;third Ventrue spear carrier from the left&quot;. But how many characters do you really need for a political campaign? When Shakespeare wrote <i>Richard III</i> he included around forty named parts. The Netflix remake of <i>House of Cards</i> contains about twenty primary characters in each of its early series. If you want to really boil it down to bare essentials you can create a political story with five characters; one in charge, two supporters (to create a majority), and two characters in opposition (because you don't want a minority of one). Of course the supporters don't necessarily support, and the opposition doesn't necessary want to overthrow the ruler. <br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter if everything ends in violence, and people die. That is, after all, what happens with <i>Richard III</i>. It can be part of the plot (or in our game terms, the chronicle). You don't want people dying all the time, and most violence shouldn't end in permanent death, having characters killed off can work to a Storyteller's advantage if done in the right manner. <br /> <br /> With all this talk about populations, participants of this forum may wish to try out an exercise. Take an American metropolitan statistical area and then design a set of characters for that MSA at a ratio of 1:100,000 for Camarilla areas, and 1:50,000 for Sabbat areas. Maybe design a few adjacent cities, and think how they might work together, and what the in-game implications of those populations might be. Think about which bits of post-revised game writing work within a universe with these populations, and what doesn't. You aren't necessarily going to stick with this version of the world within your own chronicle, but it is a worthwhile challenge to consider. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T10:47:47-07:00","id":1462138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462095#post1462095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also remind people that Chicago was always supposed to be overpopulated by vampires. From the back-cover blurb for <i>Chicago by Night:</i> <i>&amp;quot;No other city so dangerously on the edge of chaos. <b>No other city so desperately overcrowded</b>.&amp;quot;</i> Overpopulation is one of the themes of the book, and using Chicago as the yardstick for how every city in the setting is supposed to work actively goes against how the World of Darkness was portrayed in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it DID become the model, and the reason it did while how the core book did not is because Chicago by Night understood that the most important thing to any story is conflict and delivered on it by creating many external ones for PC protagonists to encounter and deal with.<br /> <br /> And external conflicts are the foundation of classical plot construction; the form most people throughout history relate best to (with any inner conflict resolved by using the external conflict as metaphor). Inner conflicts such as the quiet nightly struggle with the Beast are a distinct minority in terms of drawing interest from the population; actual studies say such storytelling appeals to less than 10% of the public\u2026 which is why film school professors will always tell students interested in telling such stories to budget appropriately and why such stories are almost invariably arthaus films on shoestring budgets\u2026 the audience just isn\u2019t there for spending more and still being able to deliver a return to your investors.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Chicago by Night defaults became the norms because external conflicts are more popular with more people than the lonely interior conflicts of 1e Core.<br /> <br /> And every external conflict is ultimately over things in limited supply; power, time, money, influence, prestige, even food in desperate times. So the best way to get conflict is for demand to exceed supply, hence vampire overpopulation is a very easy way to create conflicts because it puts pressure on everything without resorting to cartoon villainy.<br /> <br /> And pressure is where character is tested and revealed. It\u2019s easy to be a Saint in Paradise and the Beast easy to keep quiet when your belly is full and no one threatens your territory. But what someone holds to even in tough times shows who they really are.<br /> <br /> A city on the brink is where there\u2019s understandable reasons for conflicts between the generations; for why the Prince must be heavy handed and why Anarchs rail against what they feel are unjust decrees. The bad guy isn\u2019t the bad guy just because they want to twirl their mustache\u2026 they\u2019re someone who wants more than they have and is willing to go to extremes to get it.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why I believe overcrowding to the brink results in a much better setting for stories to happen than one where everyone has plenty to go around.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s certainly one of the main ways you\u2019re going to get more than academic Anarchs debating philosophy with the elders at Elysium. If everyone\u2019s fat and happy there\u2019s no need to push that hard against the status quo.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also clear the direction the setting moved towards overcrowding being more normal deliberately by the time they put The Book of Nod together since a lot of the end times passages speak of such overcrowding by the highest generations. Probably because they realizes the bit above about external conflict being a better seller.<br /> <br /> Hell, V5 leans into overcrowding even more heavily than I do. Every dot of Chasse represents just 500-1000 mortals and pages 324-5 discuss\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>\u201ca single \u2018farming\u2019 vampire needs a minimum 30 mortals to feed from to avoid anemia and other debilities in the herd, but the Masquerade is a much bigger problem when dealing with that small herds. A \u2018hunting population\u2019 should be (at minimum) two orders of magnitude larger; closer to 3000 mortals per vampire to conceal their depredations in the red noise of conventional murders, cruelties, and disappearances. Thus a coiterie of three to five vampires \u201cshould\u201d have, at minimum, a domain of 10,000 people.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Yes, that\u2019s a 1:3k minimum safe ratio you\u2019re seeing suggested in official material. V5 is not my preferred edition for a variety of reasons, but I will give them credit for understanding the need to depict a \u201ccity of adventure\u201d as the default for a campaign over the staid isolation of 1:100k.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: I looked it up and was wrong, the numbers for Chicago for 1e were 7,000,000 people supporting up to 140 vampires (so 70 excess). I for some reason thought it was 6 mil and 120 (60 excess). Still\u2026 those 70 extra came from somewhere which was my point. Easier to hunt the fringes of a major urban area than risk the Lupine filled rural regions unless things are so overcrowded even that\u2019s not an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T13:33:30-07:00","id":1462150,"title":"","content":"I think a game really only needs about 20-30 vampires for it to be robust and have enough concepts to provide plenty of hooks for most PCs. And I've certainly been in plenty of real life organizations with about that many people, and the personal or office politics can be severe. There's no problem having <i>more</i> characters, but I don't think it's <i>needed</i>. And based on observations of myself as a PC and other PCs, there's probably only around a dozen NPCs run by the ST that are essentially tracked by the PCs. Everyone else becomes part of the background. After another dozen NPCs who they interact with less frequently but know, they often can't even remember the names of the other NPCs and they simply become &quot;that guy&quot; with the one personality trait they may remember (the Prince's stooge, the Toeador's lover, the angry Brujah, or the girl with the opera gloves.) Players easily forget a lot between game sessions unless the ST reminds them. NPCs quickly become forgotten and nameless.<br /> <br /> I think the desire to view domain NPCs that number 100 or more is more do to OOC considerations tangential to running a good game than a requirement to run a good game.<br /> <br /> 1) Many STs love to design NPCs and put them into the game. They like to world build. They come up with backstories, interesting histories, motivations, etc. There's nothing wrong with that. But most of it likely never comes into play. The ST can't run each one enough to truly implant them all into the minds of the players. While players may delve into the backstories and personalities of a few NPCs, the vast majority are relegated to background roles. Players just aren't as interested in the NPCs as the STs are. So most of it is superfluous to the game.<br /> <br /> 2) STs have a desire to fill out each of the clans with appropriate concepts and numbers - they want all the clans to have enough members to showcase their diversity, feel, and generation. And then they add more clans to season the setting. So they want a variety of NPCs for each of the main clans (I will use the Camarilla here as an example). Then they may add a few members of the Independent clans or bloodlines. Put in secret Sabbat scouts. Then they realize they don't have enough Anarchs, members of this secret society, subclan, or some other faction so they fill those in. &quot;I have too many artistes and not poseurs for the Toreador they think, so they add more.&quot; But there's no reason for that distinction. It's just a legacy of &quot;that's how it's described in the Toreador clanbook so I need someone to fill that&quot;. So the numbers balloon. But in truth, most of those just aren't needed. They are there &quot;just in case&quot; something comes up and they can pull out that NPC. But most of those NPCs don't actually need to be in the domain. They could easily be moved outside the domain into a neighboring city, made a part time visitor to the domain, be a new arrival, or someone known to the domain but has to be visited.<br /> <br /> 3) Some STs think &quot;politics&quot; means sect conflicts and what side you are on. So they want all the various &quot;sides&quot; represented so they can go to war. But you don't need &quot;sides&quot; to have external conflict. Most politics are personal conflicts. Who gets what and how much. What personal slight needs to be avenged? Who gets to be top dog in this or that area? Who do I need to please to get what I want? You can have plenty of conflicts without ever introducing anyone from a different sect or side. You just need to give individual characters stakes that matter to them that are opposed by another for whatever reason. A Camarilla only city that has no threats to the sect should still have plenty of conflict between vampires. <br /> <br /> (When I use to LARP, one thing STs would often do is put the Primogen in a room to divide up the city map into feeding territory. But it was simply flavor text that meant nothing. It sounded good, but it was just bullshit and everyone knew it. It had no consequences. After the initial novelty wore off, no one cared. But when I became part of the ST staff I was able to convince them to do it differently next time. Instead of it being an exercise in flavor text, I said &quot;OK, the Prince's clan will automatically have +1 to their feeding rolls when they enter the game. That can't change. But now one additional clan also gets a +1 to their feeding challenge. One clan will get a -1. Everyone else gets no penalty and no reward. Let me know what you decide.&quot; Just making that change turned a pointless exercise into something ruthless. Not only were the Primogen really politicking with one another, the other characters not in the room became engaged too. Suddenly personal alliances and boons entered into play. Decisions mattered. <br /> <br /> (Later we figured out a way to do something similar with Influence. Draw the map to include the airport in a clan domain/feeding ground, then that got the Primogen a +1 to their Transportation influence and they could assign a -1 to someone else's influence. That little square we drew around the opera house and museum? You got it for High Society. That circle we put around the major local TV studios and newspaper? Media. This other thing got you University or Health and so on. Suddenly drawing the map became important because it wasn't just meaningless lines. Now LARP is a different animal than tabletop, and I wouldn't have a tabletop game play out like that. But it's an example of how conflict can play out even while everyone is on the same side.)<br /> <br /> Now none of the above is &quot;wrong&quot; to do. But it isn't true that it's what is required to have a good game.<br /> <br /> Published domain books will pack NPCs into them. But I think that's less because the setting requires it and more because they don't know how the STs will use the books, so they need to provide sufficient numbers, generations, etc. that can act as sires, mentors, etc. for the PCs and potential hooks for the ST. And they don't know who those PCs may be or if the ST wants to run some plot requiring a Setite, so there's a decent spread everywhere. But a custom chronicle by an ST for his gaming group doesn't need to do that.<br /> <br /> When I design and run a Camarilla chronicle (and I count Anarchs as part of that), I know I will typically want a decent number of Brujah, a fair number of Ventrue and Toreador, and a decent amount of Gangrel. That will serve most vampire concepts and the needs of the setting. But I don't need many Nosferatu, Malkavians, Tremere, or Caitiff <i>unless</i> the specific chronicle idea I have or the needs of the PCs calls for them. I don't need 10 of each. I don't need one of each generation for the clan. Hell, I don't even need all 7 clans though I do like having at least one of them. And I don't need any of the other clans, bloodlines, or sects. I include those only if I know I am going to use them. If for any reason I do end up needing an additional character to build on something the PCs are doing, I can simply place them outside the domain and allow the PCs to arrange things so they can meet someone temporarily. <br /> <br /> When I ran a Chicago chronicle, I exiled various NPCs to much smaller cities like Rockford or Peoria - not close enough to be part of Lodin's domain but not too far that they couldn't be reached. Nor did I worry that a PC might become so enamored by one of these smaller domains that they might want to leave Chicago and play the rest of the game in Peoria. I can safely put any extraneous NPCs there just in case they might be needed - the secret member of the Children of Osiris, one of the Salubri, a Giovanni, whatever. And even &quot;main&quot; Chicago NPCs like the Wolfpack might regularly visit Chicago but they don't live there. You can do similar things in most domains. <br /> <br /> That's one reason instead of doing Boston By Night, they did Dark Colony and spread out the NPCs among various cities. I don't think Dark Colony is that good of a sourcebook for various reasons, but that was something I liked about it - that since Boston, Providence, Hartford, etc. were in close proximity to each other, they were all part of the <i>same setting</i> despite being <i>different domains</i>. An ST could concentrate the PCs in one of those domains building it up (I'd probably pick Boston unless I really wanted to have a much smaller domain be the home base for whatever reason), but whenever he needed something more he could easily pull a new NPC from elsewhere or send the PCs off.<br /> <br /> The 1:100,000 rule for the metro area is arbitrary, but it works. There's no problem changing it (either by explaining why your chronicle is the exception, or ditching it for another rule), but I don't think it has any obvious weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T13:55:57-07:00","id":1462154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462095#post1462095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overpopulation is one of the themes of the book, and using Chicago as the yardstick for how every city in the setting is supposed to work actively goes against how the World of Darkness was portrayed in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but even if it was a precise overpopulation of around 60 vampires it would be a big leap to instead of brush it to a coincidence, related to it going from 1:100k to nearing 1:50k (still considered by many, me included, as a fair ratio nowadays), state that those are the vampires from Indiana and that state is virtually Kindred-free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462117#post1462117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how many characters do you really need for a political campaign?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also interesting to point out that a single character can fill multiple roles, especially if there are multiple parallel structures. The same character may have multiple functions within the city, a role in their clan structure, a position among the harpies, etc.<br /> <br /> About your exercise, maybe I'll do it, but if so I'll avoid US areas and stick to my own country, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462138#post1462138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet it DID become the model, and the reason it did while how the core book did not is because Chicago by Night understood that the most important thing to any story is conflict and delivered on it by creating many external ones for PC protagonists to encounter and deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the reason it became the norm, as stated by many others, is that <i>Revised</i> focused on institutional conflicts and started to want to fill every city with enough vampires to represent each possible faction. So you need each single big-ish city to have at least one member of each clan, preferably one of each bloodline, plus the entire &quot;Camarilla&quot; hierarchy, one or two Archons, a Sabbat pack with a priest, one Giovanni house with one Liaison to the Camarilla + Childe, and enough members of each of the Seven clans to have inner clan politics.<br /> <br /> They basically put aside the establishment of local political structures and conflicts to first guarantee that any given city will have all the Standard Official Conflicts, or SOC\u2122. That was the reason for the inflation and that stays as the sole reason for inflation.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that even then, the two versions are talking about different things. When the old books talked about 1:100k they talked about comfortable numbers, a ratio that guaranteed a safe Masquerade and that should be the target for Princes, the best scenario for the Camarilla standards, so a greater Kindred ratio means the city is considered crowded to some degree. When V5 talks about 1:3k it is talking about the absolute maximum, beyond which the Masquerade is completely impossible to sustain in the long term. More importantly, it is talking about Domain, not City.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462138#post1462138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And every external conflict is ultimately over things in limited supply</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no direct relation between this and overcrowding the city. Plenty of conflicts can still occur without overpopulation, as many things that can be disputed exist in limited supply anyways. Control over institutions, or over the best feeding grounds, knowledge, wealth. Many possible needs and wants exist that do not depend on a greater ratio of vampires to be in a short supply. Conflicts can also exist over other things, they arise from relationships not always from dispute over resources.<br /> <br /> One simple example is the game Bloodlines, that is full of conflicts between many characters, over resources and other things, and at no point the nature of those conflicts need the city to be overcrowded. And guess what? With no indication that the city have any vampire beyond the characters you meet, it has 35 Cainites even if we count the Sabbat and Giovanni present (AFAIK only one of the Giovanni is a vampire), giving LA city about... 1:100k Kindred +3 Kuei-Jin, without need to call upon the rest of LA county.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462138#post1462138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s why I believe overcrowding to the brink results in a much better setting for stories to happen than one where everyone has plenty to go around.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can keep believing that, that's not the problem. You'll make your games in crowded cities, that's ok. But there is a huge difference between favoring this kind of storytelling and stating that the setting is wrong in establishing another assumption as the default, since no game happens at a default situation to begin with, and worse with people actively telling you they manage to have good games without resorting to the same overcrowding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462138#post1462138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked it up and was wrong, the numbers for Chicago for 1e were 7,000,000 people supporting up to 140 vampires (so 70 excess).</div> </div> </div> </div>Still 1:50k, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:27:50-07:00","id":1462170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462117#post1462117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the political structures of the Ventrue laid out in the clan's revised clanbook. You have four distinct ranks of Ventrue in any given city; if you assume that there are five vampires at the top rank, each of whom oversee five vampires of the next rank (and that's about the minimum number required at a rank to make sense of the structure) you would end up with 780 Ventrue in the average city.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use the Ventrue clan hierarchy in my current chronicle. When the game began, there was one praetor, four other gerousia members, one aedile, four questors, three eirens, and one nonparticipant in the clan hierarchy, for 14 Ventrue total.<br /> <br /> The Revised clanbook doesn't give us specific numbers for how many Ventrue there should be at each rank relative to the others, but it does note that having only one aedile per city is typical, and having more than three aediles is rare in even the largest cities. Yet the book also posits the gerousia as a council/corporate board-like institution, which is only possible with least three members (otherwise they literally can't decide anything by vote, like the clanbook says they do). So we have at least one instance where a Ventrue's rank in the hierarchy isn't linked to how many Ventrue there are at the next-lowest rank.<br /> <br /> This makes sense when we look at what the ranks entail. Eirens are Ventrue who've essentially accomplished nothing their elders found noteworthy. Questors are Ventrue the elders think have shown some promise. Aediles (or more often, the aedile) serves as a spokesman and gopher for the gerousia. The gerousia are the clan &quot;elders&quot;, which is something of a misnomer, as most cities probably do not have three+ Ventrue who fit the technical and social definition of elder. <i>Chicago by Night's</i> Lodin is only ~150 years old and he's the eldest member of his clan in the city.<br /> <br /> I don't think the writers intended the Ventrue hierarchy to be an institution like the military where someone at rank X commands Y lower-ranking subordinates. The hierarchy's titles are simply tokens of a Ventrue's standing and respect among the clan. While you need some Kindred at the bottom to have others at the top, you don't need a perfectly pyramidical structure with five times as many questors as aediles.<br /> <br /> If I were to fit the Ventrue of (1e) <i>Chicago by Night</i> into the clan hierarchy, I'd probably organize them thusly:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Lodin as praetor, since he's prince and in charge of the city's other Ventrue, who are all his descendants.<br /> \u2022 Ballard and Capone are his chief lieutenants, and Neally is basically seneschal, so they fill in the rest of the gerousia. At ~150, ~100, ~100, and ~50 years dead, there aren't actually any elders on Chicago's gerousia.<br /> \u2022 Sovereign can be an aedile, as he does some pretty valuable work for the clan.<br /> \u2022 Edgar Drummond, Lorraine, Brennon Thornhill, Lawrence Ballard, and Kevin Jackson work as questors, since all of them either have a strong independent power base, a closer relationship with Lodin, or simple seniority.<br /> \u2022 The eirens can be Jacob Schumpter, Joseph Peterson, Pham Hong, and Frank Caughan, who are all largely ignored by Lodin. Ballard actually makes fun of Schumpter for how bad his financial advice is.<br /> \u2022 Tommy Hinds and Bobby Weatherbottom don't participate in the clan structure.<br /> <br /> Far from needing to come up with a long list of extraneous characters, having a pre-made social structure was helpful to me when coming up with NPCs to populate my chronicle. (Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a>, I also prefer to run sandboxy games with large casts of characters.) I considered the city's history, economy, (pop) culture, etc. when generating characters, and the Ventrue hierarchy was basically an additional source of inspiration. A &quot;skeleton&quot; into which I could fit the various Ventrue NPCs I was coming up with. The rank structure helped me flesh out the various clanmates' relationship dynamics and helped the players of Ventrue PCs understand who stood where in the clan.<br /> <br /> Some GMs may prefer a less 'institutionalized' take on the Ventrue clan and that's perfectly fine. I've known posters on this forum who preferred highly institutionalized interpretations of <i>Vampire</i> as a setting, where the Inner Circle or justicars have to officially ratify every prince of a significant city, and I've known other posters who disliked the proliferation of ranks and titles that crept into the game after 1e. But done right, I've found the later-edition political structures can enhance my chronicles and don't have to entail artificial character bloat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T17:51:42-07:00","id":1462188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462138#post1462138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet it [Chicago by Night] DID become the model</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also worth touching on. <i>Chicago by Night</i> was the game's first city sourcebook, and in the eyes of many gamers, the best one. (Definitely mine. I think only <i>Constantinople by Night </i>comes close.) So it set the standard for many of the game's concepts, even ones which were originally supposed to be unique to Chicago, or which were outright contradicted in the core rulebook. For instance...<br /> <br /> \u2022 The 1e rulebook says that Ventrue princes are supposed to be uncommon. Even though they're the leadership clan, they generally spurn that specific role. Well, obviously no one remembers that now. <i>Chicago</i> give us a Ventrue prince and Lodin set the standard for all later princes.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The city's &quot;sheriff&quot; wasn't meant to be an official position. &quot;Sheriff&quot; was just the nickname used by Balthazar, Lodin's jackbooted thug. But it clicked, and soon every city had its own sheriff, the official Darth Vader to the prince's Emperor Palpatine.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The primogen weren't supposed to be a widely-known institution. Most vampires had no clue they existed. They were a secret conspiracy behind the prince that characters needed (IIRC) a B- or higher rating in City Secrets to be aware of. But that also clicked, and soon every city had its own primogen council, and <i>Chicago by Night </i>5e softly retcons away the primogen being secret.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The primogen likewise weren't assumed to be a standard institution in cities. The Chicago primogen is implied to have evolved organically; the city's elders met to chat about issues in Elysium and realized this was a good means of resolving disputes and governing the city from behind Lodin's back. While it's equally plausible that Chicago's primogen could have formed this way in V20's much more 'institutionalized' setting, the way it's written in Chicago 1e makes it sound like the primogen are coming up with a novel idea, rather than just doing what elders in lots of Camarilla cities do.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Elysium wasn't a widespread thing either. I might be wrong on this count; I'm not sure if the 1e rulebook mentions Elysium as a concept or not. But<i> Chicago 1e</i> likewise makes it sound as if the city's vampires developed the idea on their own.<br /> <br /> Is all of this necessarily a bad thing, that other cities copied <i>Chicago by Night's</i> ideas? I don't think so. They were good ideas and writers copied them because they worked. When I designed my current chronicle's city, I was happy to have a prince, sheriff, seneschal, primogen, etc. rather than come up with a totally novel political structure. Most GMs (and sourcebook writers) aren't going to want to do that. It's easier to copy an existing model, especially when they still have tons of ways to make their city's sociopolitical setup distinct from Chicago's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462150#post1462150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one reason instead of doing Boston By Night, they did Dark Colony and spread out the NPCs among various cities. I don't think Dark Colony is that good of a sourcebook for various reasons, but that was something I liked about it - that since Boston, Providence, Hartford, etc. were in close proximity to each other, they were all part of the <i>same setting</i> despite being <i>different domains</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Colony was an interesting sourcebook. Because unlike many of the game's later ones, it didn't try to copy Chicago's political setup. Most (all?) of the princes weren't Ventrue, like the 1e rulebook said was typical. There were no primogen or sheriffs. I don't remember if there was Elysium. There were simply Anarchs, elders, and Kindred on the sides of various factions; coteries were the most important social unit in the setting. The Triad were three nominally Camarilla elders who spent most of their energy conspiring against other Camarilla vampires (and each other), but who also prosecuted war against the Sabbat and used it as pretext for taking over the cities of existing princes. There was lots of elder-elder Camarilla infighting. This was what the early game was about; internal Camarilla conflicts that didn't always involve physical violence, rather than continuous direct warfare between the Camarilla and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Next to Chicago, I agree that Dark Colony was a fairly weak sourcebook. But it had some cool ideas. (Another neat one was that the methuselahs behind the Triad weren't actually located in New England, which highlighted the global nature of their interests.) I think if Dark Colony had been more popularly received, we would have seen more sourcebooks that attempted more novel political setups, or at least sought to emulate Dark Colony's alongside Chicago's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 09-30-2021, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:52:06-07:00","id":1462197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462188#post1462188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next to Chicago, I agree that Dark Colony was a fairly weak sourcebook. But it had some cool ideas. (Another neat one was that the methuselahs behind the Triad weren't actually located in New England, which highlighted the global nature of their interests.) I think if Dark Colony had been more popularly received, we would have seen more sourcebooks that attempted more novel political setups, or at least sought to emulate Dark Colony's alongside Chicago's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Colony had most of the same flaws that subsequent By Night books had.<br /> <br /> 1) Lower page count than Chicago By Night so a lot less space to develop the setting.<br /> <br /> 2) A large section of the book was taken over by a single railroad introductory &quot;story&quot;. Chicago By Night had no such thing just pages of many different plot ideas. Longer &quot;stories&quot; were produced in its companion book, the Succubus Club. So Dark Colony had about 60 pages to develop its setting compared to Chicago having over 160. Those extra hundred pages make a big difference.<br /> <br /> 3) More non-vampire stuff is crowding out vampire content. We get more details on Lupines, Mage covens, and the like. If you like that sort of thing, it's fine. Unfortunately it is poor integrated into the setting. We're told what's there, but not how that may affect vampires in the setting except in the broadest terms. It's the kind of filler not found in Chicago.<br /> <br /> 4) A rather uninteresting hook. Did anyone really care about the whole British Kindred invading America concept in a replay of the American Revolution? I don't know anyone who felt inspired by that. It's a shame because there's already a strong hook buried there - this sourcebook should be teaching us how the Sabbat and Camarilla fight each other for control of an area.<br /> <br /> 5) The book is poorly organized for its presentation. Dark Colony should essentially be organized around the separate major domains of the region, with other domains left open to ST development. We should get an idea of how Quentin King III rules Boston, and Upton Rowlands rules New Haven/Hartford. Roman Pendragon is the Prince of Concord who rules over all New Hampshire. And Warwick is presumably the Prince of Providence. It seems like there should be other petty princes around the region, but we're given nothing except estimated numbers of vampires per state. For some of these cities, one coterie chart would be the <i>entire</i> domain. We could have used those extra hundred pages to briefly develop each domain separately and how their vampires interact with one another as a collective whole as well. Likewise we're given the names of two Sabbat packs and their leaders, but that's it. So as a tool for the ST, it's hampered.<br /> <br /> I do agree it has some cool ideas. I like Warwick's Web, the Gemini League, Boston as a Malkavian center of power, roving Sabbat packs, and certain characters. But if I was ever going to run a Dark Colony chronicle, I think I'd have to decide what elements I wanted to include in it, discard the book as a whole except as an idea mine, and build an entirely new chronicle using those few stones I took for the rubble and brand new ideas of my own. That's a lot of work. Doing that much work is not why I purchase a sourcebook. In contrast, almost everyone can run Chicago By Night out of the box which is why I think it's the most popular By Night book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T07:00:45-07:00","id":1462276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1462197#post1462197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) A rather uninteresting hook. Did anyone really care about the whole British Kindred invading America concept in a replay of the American Revolution? I don't know anyone who felt inspired by that. It's a shame because there's already a strong hook buried there - this sourcebook should be teaching us how the Sabbat and Camarilla fight each other for control of an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was one of the worst parts of the book for me. It came off as a parody of New England culture--Midwestern writers knew the region as &quot;where the American Revolution happened&quot;, so they seemingly thought, &quot;Hey, let's have a central conflict that parallels the American Revolution!&quot; They tried to force it even further with followers of the Triad being known as &quot;Redcoats&quot; and playing up Anglophobic sentiment among the region's native Kindred, and it just felt completely farcial. It felt like the writers didn't care about any of New England's history and culture after the American Revolution.<br /> <br /> The basic idea of three foreign elders invading Camarilla domains in New England isn't inherently problematic. I'd just remove the forced Anglophobia and stop framing the conflict in terms of British vs. Americans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do agree it has some cool ideas. I like Warwick's Web, the Gemini League, Boston as a Malkavian center of power, roving Sabbat packs, and certain characters. </div> </div> </div>I also liked the Web, and have even used it in my own games. I liked the Triad's members. I liked the methuselahs behind the Triad, and I liked them not actually being located in New England, which helped distinguish them from Helena and Menele. I liked Elsa Linden and her tie to Annabelle Triabelle. I liked Upton Rowlands as a snooty WASP Ventrue with ties to Yale. I like the idea of roving Sabbat packs in rural Maine--basically fodder for Stephen King stories in the WoD.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of the NPCs were as good as Chicago's, but they were good enough. It's just that 100 fewer pages of content, as you note, really kneecaps the book's potential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:16:17-07:00","id":1464060,"title":"","content":"Upped because this is a good thread for the Anarch discussion in the Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> REPOSTED:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1463946#post1463946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this was the <i>intention</i> of the original writers that the Anarchs would be the default PC faction for some of the reasons you gave. But I don't think that's what actually <i>happened</i>. From my personal experience of the early days (which of course is extremely limited but I have no reason to think it was an exception), players did in fact initially gravitate to Anarch type PCs because the initial presentation of the game encouraged it. Certainly Chicago By Night encouraged PCs to be enemies of Lodin. Most of us were coming from combat heavy RPGs, and it seemed like this is what we were supposed to do.<br /> <br /> But quite early on, players started defecting away from the Anarch stereotype. They became much more interested in aspects of Vampire that took them away from being adolescent hoodlums angry at the Man. Not everyone wanted their PC to be in the movie The Lost Boys. They had other inspirations. The moment the first player brought the clanbook or players guide they just bought, interest in playing Anarch-type PCs declined.<br /> <br /> They wanted to roleplay the interesting aspects of their clan's culture. They wanted to explore Elysium and salon culture of the elders. As more of the game setting was introduced in the Clanbooks and Players Guide, the less interested players were to be on the anarch side of things. They found the aspects associated with the Camarilla and the elders much <i>more</i> interesting. Players wanted to explore that. They couldn't explore those aspects of the setting well if they were actually Anarchs because Anarchs were expected to reject all of that.<br /> <br /> The players who wanted to play Ventrue and Tremere were usually never interested in being Anarchs at all. And once more of the setting was explored, I saw the clans of the Toreador, Malkavians, and Nosferatu drop interest among the Anarchs. I really only saw many, but not all, of the Brujah PC players truly want to play Anarch characters.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the PCs might still want to overthrow Lodin. But it wasn't so they could free the young and powerless vampires from the tyranny of the elders. It was to put one of the PCs (or a trusted NPC ally) as Prince instead which is a big difference.<br /> <br /> From what I personally experienced, the Anarch phase of most tabletop games lasted about three months until the ST and PCs learned enough about the setting to move on to things they found much more interesting. Then they rebooted their chronicles.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying all players did so. I know some Vampire players that were interested in playing only Anarch PCs or at least PCs that were sympathetic to the Anarchs. And the Brujah Anarch archetype was certainly a popular PC choice. But they were a distinct minority in most gaming groups, and had to adjust to most of their gaming group just wasn't interested in going down that route. I'm sure there were plenty of games where the players and STs were mostly interested on the Anarch side of things, but I don't think they were representative.<br /> <br /> Likewise the LARPs I attended that were Anarch based were less well regarded than those that were Camarilla. Anarch LARPs quickly succumbed to the problem of no one knowing what to do with the setting. Things quickly became repetitive, especially if the Prince was gone and the setting was now a Free State. On the other hand, the Camarilla games have enough variety of aspects to them that more players found things to do.<br /> <br /> I think one reason some players were really looking forward to LAbN originally was there was the hope that Anarch centric games could be just as interesting to explore as Camarilla games. We just needed to know what was in the secret sauce in the mysterious Anarch Free State! Then we found out it was bland and uninteresting. The main thing that made the Anarchs interesting to play was putting them in contrast to the rest of the vampire culture overseen by the Camarilla. Players might want their PCs to have feet in both worlds to a degree to explore as much of the setting as possible, but I didn't see most choosing to play Anarchs. It's a totally valid choice to do so, and I do want the game to have better toolkits to help STs run those kind of chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Evolving Nature of the Anarchs, Traditions, and Rebellion</b><br /> <br /> I have some theories about the larger societal context regarding the Anarchs in V:TM and Mage: The Ascension's Traditions. My view is the Anarchs were very popular in the early Nineties as a continuation of cyberpunk and its themes from the 80s. Reaganomics and Thatcherism leading to the creation of the counter-culture movement against the unchecked greed as well as rising authoritarianism of the period. However, V:TM's take was a supernatural themed Punk setting that came at the tail end of the cultural movement.<br /> <br /> However, the Nineties was a time that had a backlash against the Punk and anti-authoritarianism of the Eighties. REALITY BITES and other works of the period emphasized that with the fall of the Soviet Union and triumph of capitalism as well as seemingly democracy, it was the &quot;End of History&quot; and seemingly nothing to worry about. Rebellion against &quot;The Man&quot; seemed adolescent and silly rather than a recognition of horrid inequalities in the system.<br /> <br /> Hence the shift went from the Camarilla as the bad guys to the Sabbat who were a more overt and militant threat you could shoot in the face.<br /> <br /> I attribute to this the general whitewashing and slow change of the Technocracy from an embodiment of the evils of capitalism and colonialism to the &quot;one true champions&quot; of the human race against the evil supernaturals. The Technocracy embodying Western hegemonic power and rampant techology was greeted by many aging players as, &quot;Why the hell not?&quot; That, of course, was before the War on Terror, Recession, and other elements that I think may be a major reason why Paradox has chosen to lean into the Anarchs HARD. A lot of the systemic corruption and abuses of power in the world are once more in the public mindset.<br /> <br /> I'm also of the mind that Anarchs are something that is inherently better for tabletop gaming than LARP. Larp is very much about the pageantry and social combat element of the game and that is something that loud, angry, revolution-based games are not going to be able to do nearly as well. Same for why you don't see many cyberpunk LARPS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-15-2021, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T13:47:57-07:00","id":1464081,"title":"","content":"Some bits by Justin Achilli:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013445647548417 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1449013931515813891 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anarchs are the default sect for V5 and going way back. The Camarilla became the default for V2-V20. Anarchs are especially popular among new and young players. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WoD5 also has as thematic element across all games, in that status quo/ world as it is is an &quot;antagonist,&quot; and Anarchs are inherently at odds with that. (Werewolves also oppose exploitative status quo, Hunters at odds with status-quo orgs like the SAD, Society of St. Leo, etc. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:15:39-07:00","id":1464092,"title":"","content":"Justin Achilli has some really good insight, and more importantly, a good vision for WoD as whole, whether we personally like it or not it seems that a good organization of the setting's elements is one of his priorities. Which is something I think is always crucial for a multi-setting game world like WoD.<br /> <br /> Either way, those discussions about the Anarchs, and Camarilla default, and Sabbat, and gamer public and interest changing with the decades was really interesting to read and think about. <br /> And I mean, although the V5 Anarch book does show a lot of interesting ways the sect organizes itself in different cities, it is way to small a vision of each, like small snapshots, that don't help in using that as your own as much as it should. It was more of a collage of different nitbits, with very little crunch (and it doesn't need actual mechanics to be so in this case). Like, chapters about the history of the movement, the daily unlife and the positions vampires take or organize themselves in the domain was the most useful of the bunch (for me). The other one that comes into mind is the castle resort of rich Cainites, which is a very different and interesting way of going Anarch; also, the one where the gang style events are barely not Sabbat, where people stab and shoot each other, basking in their immortality. The rest I don't remember well. <br /> Anarchs should be an idea circus, with some common denominators but being pretty unique and fun. But without being at the opposite side of the table where the Camarilla is sited, it is just a hollow amorphous sect (and yeah I know, Anarch isn't much a sect as it is a movement and all that). So what defines Anarchs end up being &quot;not being Camarilla&quot; and &quot;not being Sabbat&quot;, which is... kinda of useless. Sure anarch and anarchy is kind of no &quot;order&quot;, but it is technically no hierarchy, not plain chaos. The work of the writers of WoD should be to pump action and event inside the Anarchs dominion; not just put them as &quot;man I hate that Camarilla over there&quot;. Their interaction with Hecata, the Brujah Council in Russia, their &quot;acceptance&quot; of the Ministry (as much as not baring them from existing as their neighbors I imagine), all these are little bits that give interesting things to the Anarch game, but it still lacks the inner drama. It is almost no surprise that almost every game and comic of Vampire is about a fledgling Embraced without permission in a Camarilla territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:36:23-07:00","id":1464096,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna re-post what said in the Sabbat topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So for instance, my Anarch faction that's trying to take control of Glasgow is mostly made from some local gangs and ex-Sabbat packs led by a Child of the Dracon Tzimisce. They are trying to fulfill the Dream by making Glasgow the &quot;Carthage of the North.&quot; The way they plan to do this is to apply the Vaulderie to not just every kindred in the city, but also, eventually, when the time is right, apply it to every kine as well. Then there is also a bunch of Ministry influence (who claim to be the original religion of Carthage) and a bunch of conflict with the Camarilla in Edinburgh, which of course is all about the Cult of Mithras.<br /> <br /> Basically I'm trying to make the sect feel as flavourful and unique as possible, which tbf kind of ends up being a &quot;kinder&quot; Sabbat with the numbers filed off. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T18:24:26-07:00","id":1464119,"title":"","content":"In any given city, the Anarchs are one vampire who wants to be Prince but doesn't have the connections or the competence for traditional city politics, and an army of the disaffected and the powerless who he's flim-flammed with promises to cater to their resentments.<br /> <br /> And the devil of it is: if the Free States ever finally fail, it will be because MacNeil was too afraid of being promoted beyond his competence to be that guy and wield that praxis.<br /> <br /> I love me some political horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 10-15-2021, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T23:13:11-07:00","id":1464157,"title":"","content":"This spin-off discussion about population, overcrowding and urban areas is really interesting.<br /> <br /> The italian urban landscape is very different from the American one: there are only a few big cities (in American sense, only Rome, Naples and Milan, with Bologna and Turin coming close, are big cities of over 1 million inhabitants between the main city and neighbouring sprawls), and a huge chunk of the population lives in small-to-medium towns, and commutes daily, as distances aren't huge.<br /> <br /> So you rarely find huge urban sprawls hwere you get lost, but it's also really rare to have isolated houses in the middle of nowhere. It's more like there's always someone next door.<br /> <br /> I've always wondered how a post-apocalyptic scenario would play out in Italy, as basically everyone can take a bike and reach the closest city, and you can probably reach a bigger urban center in a hour.<br /> <br /> Most of these cities and towns date to roman or medieval, so they are extremely packed with interesting story hooks: my Region, Marche, is placed in the central part of the country and has only 1.5 million inhabitants, but it hosts two ports and one airport, 4 universities, two former ducal cities one of whom, Urbino, is a UNESCO Heritage site, and countless smaller cities with centuries' odl feuds and alliances.<br /> <br /> Were I to apply the classic 1:100.000 ratio, there would be 15 vampires in the whole region, but there is a lot of narrative potential: if we pick Ancona, the regioin capital, we have a 100.000 people city who hosts a Polytechnic University, an important theatre the main regional Hospital, the regional government and regional industrial unions. This definitely screams &quot;<i>High Clans and Camarilla</i>&quot;, but Ancona is also the seat of a port and naval shipyard with a strong trade union bent, it has hosted two important revolutionary uprisings (the Red Week of 1914 and a military revolt in 1920) and had a strong masonic presence (it still has it), so you can definitely play Anarchs too, and in Clan terms can range anywhere from Tremere to Brujah.<br /> <br /> In the Middle Ages it was an ally of the Pope against the Empire and of Byzantium against Venice, and it was besieged by a Staufen-Venetian coalition led by Federico Barbarossa. All the neighbouring cities have allied against its power at least once.<br /> <br /> It would take a whole court to give justice to all the potential plot hooks and inspirations, and then you would also need rival courts in neighbouring cities.<br /> <br /> When we did LARP, in my small city of 30.000, we embraced this approach, and went with the &quot;reconstructed overcrowded domain populated by ambitious ancillae and estranged neonates&quot;, and one of the main political plots was the fight for hunting grounds and hegemony with the princes of Ancona, Pesaro and Urbino, and Perugia, which eventually drew in the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-16-2021, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T02:23:59-07:00","id":1464164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460472-world-building-how-do-you-do-the-anarchs?p=1464157#post1464157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The italian urban landscape is very different from the American one: there are only a few big cities (in American sense, only Rome, Naples and Milan, with Bologna and Turin coming close, are big cities of over 1 million inhabitants between the main city and neighbouring sprawls), and a huge chunk of the population lives in small-to-medium towns, and commutes daily, as distances aren't huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>By my take, this would mean that most vampire courts are spread through an area instead of the strict interpretation of One City, One Prince.<br /> <br /> Looking on G-Maps it says that you can go from San Benedetto del Tronto to Lamoli by car in about 2 and a half hours through Autostrada Adriatica (or 3hs through Statale 77 to avoid tolls), please correct if this is wrong. If it isn't, then you can basically traverse the entirety of Marche in a night and still have plenty of time before the sunrise, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Under such conditions, an ambitious Prince could try and claim domain over the entire region. This would be a stretched domain, but doable. And since they're so integrated in so many levels, even with princes for each province it is probable that envoys are common as are conflicts between the courts.<br /> <br /> I don't think you need 150 vampires to play this. As immortals with clearly defined lineages vampires can inherit a lot of historic background. Each character is already full of references by themselves, their lineages and their past acquaintances. Of course, since you attend LARPs you have to consider how many people will show up to actually play, but I do think that a baseline of 30 is enough to build the entire network, 15 is perfectly doable if you want a game that plays on the insular nature of Kindred, 50 is plenty (and a ratio of 1:30k, quite crowded but not by a factor of 10).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:36:57-07:00","id":1464189,"title":"","content":"Thinking about population starts to get weird for me when you consider that there are more people in London alone than there is in the entirety of Scotland. So Camden moving the Cult of Mithras and the remains of his court to Edinburgh is a massive shift of kindred into that area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}